WEBVTT

00:15.015 --> 00:17.016
[theme music playing]

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:03.021 --> 01:04.189
[Seung-hyo] The women's dorm?

01:05.106 --> 01:05.940
Are you insane?

01:06.024 --> 01:07.734
You want me to sneak into
the women's dorm?

01:07.817 --> 01:08.693
What's the problem?

01:08.777 --> 01:11.029
My roommates
always sneak their boyfriends in.

01:11.112 --> 01:13.615
So? You want me to play
drinking games with them?

01:13.698 --> 01:16.284
Should we? They love drinking games here.

01:16.367 --> 01:18.244
Hey, I taught them how to play Mafia.

01:18.328 --> 01:19.996
-They're good.
-Hey!

01:20.080 --> 01:22.165
Don't worry. They're not here.

01:22.749 --> 01:24.459
-So you're alone?
-[Seok-ryu] Yeah.

01:26.461 --> 01:27.837
Hey, where are you going?

01:27.921 --> 01:30.924
The bars nearby aren't even open late.

01:31.007 --> 01:32.133
They're expensive too.

01:32.217 --> 01:34.844
It'll be my treat in my room!

01:34.928 --> 01:37.764
Our little baby can save
his allowance and buy snacks.

01:37.847 --> 01:38.681
Get off me.

01:38.765 --> 01:42.769
Right. Now that you're in the US,
what do you want to do the most?

01:45.230 --> 01:46.898
Let's think about it later. Come on!

01:46.981 --> 01:49.108
Let's go and get wasted!

01:49.192 --> 01:50.610
I don't think this is right.

01:51.319 --> 01:52.987
Okay. You look so pretty!

01:53.071 --> 01:54.656
You look like a girl. Let's go.

01:54.739 --> 01:55.740
[indistinct chatter]

01:56.616 --> 01:57.617
[birds chirping]

02:03.957 --> 02:04.958
[groans softly]

02:09.379 --> 02:10.463
[groans]

02:16.386 --> 02:17.303
[groans]

02:20.598 --> 02:21.808
Damn.

02:35.655 --> 02:36.948
[pleasant music playing]

02:40.243 --> 02:41.077
[inhales]

02:50.336 --> 02:53.006
[Seok-ryu] What do you want to do
the most here in US?

02:53.089 --> 02:54.090
You dummy.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.342
Why do you think I'm here?

03:00.305 --> 03:01.723
[phone vibrating]

03:01.806 --> 03:04.100
DID YOU FORGET ABOUT OUR DATE TODAY?

03:10.899 --> 03:12.400
[Seok-ryu] My head hurts.

03:14.360 --> 03:15.862
I have a splitting headache.

03:20.283 --> 03:22.702
What? When did you get up?

03:22.785 --> 03:25.330
-What? Right…
-[Seok-ryu clears throat]

03:25.413 --> 03:26.706
Just now.

03:27.290 --> 03:28.458
[coughs]

03:29.334 --> 03:31.377
I think you got a text.

03:31.461 --> 03:32.295
Really?

03:33.630 --> 03:34.547
[Seung-hyo exclaims]

03:35.465 --> 03:36.341
[Seok-ryu groans]

03:42.305 --> 03:43.139
[chuckles softly]

03:43.848 --> 03:44.682
Who is it?

03:44.766 --> 03:45.892
My boyfriend.

03:46.643 --> 03:47.560
[mellow music playing]

03:48.311 --> 03:50.313
I'm seeing him later. Come with me.

03:50.939 --> 03:52.649
You have a boyfriend now?

03:52.732 --> 03:55.485
Yeah, we just started dating.

03:55.568 --> 03:57.654
His name's Brian. He's an overseas Korean.

03:57.737 --> 03:59.989
He can't speak Korean that well.
It's so cute.

04:00.073 --> 04:01.824
[chuckles] He can barely spell.

04:05.078 --> 04:09.332
Gosh, he's so adorable!
He can't even spell "promise" right!

04:18.174 --> 04:20.218
Jeez, why is it so dark in here?

04:20.301 --> 04:21.886
Just be quiet for a second.

04:21.970 --> 04:24.222
I'm sure the switch
is around here somewhere.

04:24.305 --> 04:27.267
[Seok-ryu] You built this building,
but you can't even find the lights?

04:27.976 --> 04:29.143
[Seung-hyo] I found it.

04:29.811 --> 04:30.979
-[Seok-ryu yelps]
-[groans]

04:35.275 --> 04:37.527
You're a habitual offender.

04:39.237 --> 04:43.116
It was a normal reaction to avoid falling.

04:43.199 --> 04:44.367
Habitual offender, my foot.

04:44.450 --> 04:46.035
Then, what was that earlier?

04:46.119 --> 04:47.245
My gosh!

04:51.791 --> 04:53.293
Give it.

04:58.464 --> 05:01.426
If you go to Namsan,
aren't you supposed to have pork cutlets?

05:01.509 --> 05:02.677
Why did you buy groceries?

05:02.760 --> 05:06.639
Hey, you're supposed to cook food
on a good day like this.

05:06.723 --> 05:08.266
Just wait, okay?

05:08.349 --> 05:11.311
I'll show you a pretty cook,
as if there's "Something in the Rain."

05:11.394 --> 05:13.313
Seriously though,
don't mess with Son Ye-jin.

05:18.234 --> 05:19.819
[pleasant music playing]

05:27.243 --> 05:28.119
Want some help?

05:29.329 --> 05:30.413
You know how to cook?

05:32.040 --> 05:33.207
Just go and sit.

05:44.177 --> 05:45.344
Why are you so good?

05:46.345 --> 05:49.140
I was ready to call Mo-eum
in case you cut a finger off.

06:29.972 --> 06:30.932
[music fades]

06:31.933 --> 06:35.019
The food is… so green.

06:35.561 --> 06:37.188
It's colorful like grass.

06:37.271 --> 06:39.941
Is that all you can say?

06:40.024 --> 06:44.278
You took my pork cutlets, so I expected
at least some spicy stir-fried pork.

06:44.362 --> 06:46.197
You have a palate of a child.

06:46.280 --> 06:49.325
People should eat seasonal food.

06:49.408 --> 06:52.954
Especially, spring greens.
They're just as good as wild ginseng.

06:53.037 --> 06:55.498
There you go embellishing again,
like MSG on food.

06:58.584 --> 06:59.418
[exclaims]

07:05.550 --> 07:08.052
No, that's actual MSG.
What did you put in here?

07:08.136 --> 07:09.887
-Powdered stock?
-My cooking skills.

07:09.971 --> 07:12.265
No way. Why is it so good?

07:12.890 --> 07:14.600
Is it good? Really?

07:20.356 --> 07:21.190
[clears throat]

07:22.150 --> 07:24.318
I know what it is. Yeah.

07:24.402 --> 07:28.448
I'm so hungry right now
that I can't be objective.

07:28.531 --> 07:30.825
I should've just pushed you
off that mountain.

07:30.908 --> 07:32.618
Let me eat before you kill me.

07:32.702 --> 07:33.828
At least I'll be full.

07:36.164 --> 07:38.541
-[exclaims]
-It's honestly good though, right?

07:38.624 --> 07:39.584
Not bad, right?

07:42.587 --> 07:43.838
[pleasant music playing]

07:44.630 --> 07:45.631
[chimes]

07:45.715 --> 07:47.592
[heart beating]

07:49.093 --> 07:50.052
[chimes]

07:51.888 --> 07:53.139
[coughs]

07:54.140 --> 07:56.434
Hey, don't eat so fast.

07:57.226 --> 07:58.060
[coughs, groans]

07:58.769 --> 08:00.688
[Mo-eum] Wow, that smells great!

08:00.771 --> 08:01.606
What's this?

08:01.689 --> 08:03.983
-[gasps]
-I showcased my talents a little.

08:04.066 --> 08:05.735
Why are you so late?

08:05.818 --> 08:08.362
I'm a civil servant.

08:08.446 --> 08:09.655
I was busy with my duties.

08:10.239 --> 08:12.033
You did a great job.

08:12.116 --> 08:13.910
I'll go and buy some drinks.

08:13.993 --> 08:15.536
[Mo-eum] What? Okay.

08:19.081 --> 08:21.375
Why is he leaving so suddenly?

08:21.459 --> 08:23.169
I don't know.

08:23.252 --> 08:25.046
-I don't know.
-Eat up.

08:25.129 --> 08:26.547
Okay. It looks so good.

08:26.631 --> 08:28.216
[coughing]

08:28.299 --> 08:29.509
[quirky music playing]

08:30.384 --> 08:31.219
Darn it.

08:32.470 --> 08:35.014
Why is Seok-ryu
suddenly looking at me weird like that?

08:36.807 --> 08:39.268
She usually looks mad,
but now her eyes look kind.

08:41.479 --> 08:43.523
They're too round and kind.

08:45.316 --> 08:46.150
[exhales]

08:47.860 --> 08:49.737
It looks so good.

08:49.820 --> 08:50.905
-[phone vibrating]
-Eat up.

08:50.988 --> 08:51.864
Hold on.

08:53.449 --> 08:54.534
MOM

08:55.117 --> 08:56.619
It's okay.

08:56.702 --> 08:58.162
I'll do it.

08:58.246 --> 08:59.705
Why didn't you answer your mom?

08:59.789 --> 09:01.666
What? Because I know what she'll say.

09:03.000 --> 09:04.877
She wants me to go on a blind date.

09:04.961 --> 09:06.295
-Really?
-[Mo-eum] Yeah.

09:07.296 --> 09:09.382
My mom suffered so much from her in-laws.

09:09.465 --> 09:11.717
Why does she want me
to get married so badly?

09:13.052 --> 09:14.095
You know what happened.

09:14.178 --> 09:15.972
After my dad died when I was seven,

09:16.055 --> 09:19.475
my grandma went crazy
and blamed my mom for his death.

09:19.559 --> 09:20.851
That's why we moved here.

09:21.435 --> 09:22.520
I know.

09:22.603 --> 09:24.855
I swear, I just don't get it.

09:24.939 --> 09:27.316
-Marriage isn't always the answer.
-Right.

09:27.400 --> 09:28.276
You're right.

09:28.359 --> 09:31.070
That's why I ran away
before going through with things.

09:35.700 --> 09:37.660
There is one regret though.

09:37.743 --> 09:40.580
I wanted to see you in a wedding dress.

09:41.163 --> 09:44.083
What? You can see.
Want to see my wedding photos?

09:44.166 --> 09:46.252
-You haven't deleted them yet?
-[Seok-ryu] No.

09:46.335 --> 09:48.504
I spent a fortune
and put in so much effort.

09:48.588 --> 09:50.006
How could I delete them?

09:51.257 --> 09:52.133
[Mo-eum exclaims]

09:52.883 --> 09:55.595
Wow. You're so pretty.

09:55.678 --> 09:57.138
[Seok-ryu] I think so too.

09:58.639 --> 10:01.058
[Mo-eum] What? What's this?

10:01.142 --> 10:04.228
It's the smile you make
when you're truly happy.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.647
I know who took this picture.

10:14.196 --> 10:15.072
Hey.

10:16.449 --> 10:21.037
I'm going to figure out
why you two broke up.

10:22.204 --> 10:23.205
So?

10:25.207 --> 10:27.084
Are you okay now?

10:28.461 --> 10:30.755
Have you completely moved on from him?

10:33.424 --> 10:34.425
No.

10:35.301 --> 10:36.510
I still love him.

10:37.303 --> 10:38.971
[mellow music playing]

10:40.556 --> 10:41.807
[footsteps approaching]

10:42.933 --> 10:45.811
Gosh, I left my wallet.

10:45.895 --> 10:47.146
I had to come all the way back.

10:47.897 --> 10:50.191
Hey, you're all okay with beer, right?

10:50.274 --> 10:51.901
No, I want soju tonight.

10:51.984 --> 10:53.194
I want to get drunk.

10:53.277 --> 10:55.613
-Okay. Got it.
-I want non-alcoholic beer.

10:55.696 --> 10:58.783
-And juice.
-[Mo-eum] What? Why?

10:59.533 --> 11:02.953
No, you're right. Don't get drunk tonight.
That'll be safer.

11:03.704 --> 11:05.748
[Seung-hyo] Don't eat until I get back.
Wait for me.

11:05.831 --> 11:07.249
Don't you dare lay a finger.

11:17.301 --> 11:18.594
[bell dinging]

11:21.680 --> 11:22.932
[birds chirping]

11:35.945 --> 11:37.738
[exhales, inhales]

11:42.701 --> 11:43.911
[exhales]

11:43.994 --> 11:47.456
[Mi-suk] Look at her.
Her legs are shaking.

11:47.540 --> 11:48.916
[quirky music playing]

11:51.252 --> 11:52.086
[all laughing]

11:52.169 --> 11:53.754
Her legs are totally exhausted.

11:53.838 --> 11:57.007
Why did you want to start
the morning with 108 prostrations?

11:57.633 --> 12:00.636
We can't be doing that at our age.
Your knees will give out.

12:00.719 --> 12:03.764
[panting] Stop. Goodness.

12:04.557 --> 12:06.600
As long as my son can pass his exams,

12:06.684 --> 12:09.603
they can take both my knees
and make stew with them!

12:09.687 --> 12:12.189
-[Jae-suk chuckles]
-You can't say that at a temple.

12:12.273 --> 12:15.192
Buddhists are vegetarians.
Don't you know they only eat vegetables?

12:15.276 --> 12:18.320
Hey, it was just a joke.

12:18.404 --> 12:19.780
Are you upset about something?

12:20.364 --> 12:22.491
-No, I'm not.
-Are you sure?

12:22.575 --> 12:24.994
That's not what your face is saying.

12:25.995 --> 12:27.413
What's wrong with my face?

12:27.496 --> 12:29.331
Why are you picking on an innocent person?

12:29.415 --> 12:32.751
Hey, don't raise your voice
in front of Buddha.

12:32.835 --> 12:34.378
Let's go do what we always do.

12:34.462 --> 12:36.505
What? Lunch?

12:36.589 --> 12:37.882
[Hye-suk] Where are we eating?

12:37.965 --> 12:38.966
[both chuckling]

12:40.009 --> 12:42.052
Something's up with her.

12:42.136 --> 12:43.387
[Mi-suk] Hey.

12:46.307 --> 12:47.475
Hey, take this.

12:49.935 --> 12:53.606
-These are prayer tiles.
-[groans softly]

12:53.689 --> 12:55.941
My son needs to pass his exams

12:56.025 --> 12:57.776
before all of these tiles are used.

12:57.860 --> 12:59.612
Have you ever done this before?

12:59.695 --> 13:01.363
-I've seen it before.
-[Mi-suk scoffs]

13:01.447 --> 13:02.656
Do I write with this?

13:02.740 --> 13:03.949
[Mi-suk] Yeah, go ahead.

13:08.037 --> 13:10.789
PARK KI-HOON
PASS THE CIVIL SERVICE EXAM

13:10.873 --> 13:11.707
[sniffles]

13:14.460 --> 13:16.962
MO-EUM
MOVE OUT

13:17.046 --> 13:18.380
BAE GEUN-SIK
FIND BUSINESS SUCCESS

13:18.464 --> 13:20.925
BAE SEOK-RYU

13:27.473 --> 13:31.769
BAE SEOK-RYU
RETURN TO ORIGINAL STATE

13:44.406 --> 13:45.366
[Hye-suk exhales]

13:47.660 --> 13:48.827
"Move out"?

13:48.911 --> 13:49.954
Hey.

13:50.037 --> 13:51.205
You want Mo-eum to be a monk?

13:51.288 --> 13:52.206
Hey!

13:52.289 --> 13:53.832
-What?
-Seriously?

13:53.916 --> 13:55.709
It doesn't mean that.

13:55.793 --> 13:58.587
She's talking about marriage.

13:58.671 --> 14:01.257
-I see!
-[Jae-suk] For crying out loud.

14:01.340 --> 14:03.509
LET MY SON FORGET THAT MEMORY
LET ME RECONCILE WITH HIM

14:03.592 --> 14:05.761
You're showing off
on a whole new level now.

14:05.844 --> 14:07.263
You wrote it in French?

14:07.346 --> 14:09.265
It just happened by chance.

14:09.348 --> 14:10.558
And it comes more naturally.

14:10.641 --> 14:11.600
Yeah, right.

14:11.684 --> 14:13.060
She doesn't want us to read it.

14:13.143 --> 14:14.937
It's not that.

14:15.020 --> 14:18.941
But all of our wishes are
for our husbands and children.

14:19.024 --> 14:20.234
[In-suk] What else can we do?

14:20.317 --> 14:23.946
These scoundrels need to do well
for us to be at peace.

14:24.029 --> 14:25.614
You're right.

14:25.698 --> 14:27.032
[Jae-suk] These scoundrels.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.617
Return to your original state!

14:28.701 --> 14:29.577
Move out.

14:29.660 --> 14:31.203
Pass the exam!

14:31.287 --> 14:32.246
A productive human.

14:36.834 --> 14:37.751
[music fades]

14:37.835 --> 14:40.212
[Geun-sik] Professor!

14:40.296 --> 14:41.547
Are you going to work?

14:41.630 --> 14:43.883
-I'm coming home from work.
-You work so hard.

14:43.966 --> 14:46.760
Do you want to eat something
before you go in?

14:46.844 --> 14:48.429
Your wife's likely not home.

14:48.512 --> 14:49.847
-What?
-The Suk Sisters…

14:49.930 --> 14:51.557
Wait, they changed their name. [laughs]

14:51.640 --> 14:53.517
They're Lavender now.

14:53.601 --> 14:56.645
Anyway, they went on
an overnight trip together.

14:56.729 --> 14:58.355
They went to a temple.

14:58.439 --> 15:00.190
But my wife's a Catholic.

15:00.274 --> 15:02.067
-What?
-Nothing.

15:02.151 --> 15:04.528
I'm a bit tired. I'll eat next time.

15:04.612 --> 15:06.530
Okay, goodbye.

15:06.614 --> 15:07.781
Wait!

15:07.865 --> 15:09.742
Let's get another drink next time.

15:09.825 --> 15:11.201
[chuckles]

15:11.285 --> 15:13.454
Sir, are you open?

15:13.537 --> 15:14.663
Yes, of course!

15:14.747 --> 15:16.540
-Okay.
-I'll see you next time.

15:16.624 --> 15:18.584
-[boy 1] Places like this still exist?
-Come in!

15:18.667 --> 15:19.543
Look at the sign.

15:19.627 --> 15:20.920
-[boy 1] Wow!
-[exhales]

15:21.003 --> 15:22.421
[boy 2] Record that.

15:25.674 --> 15:28.052
-[Geun-sik] Here's your food.
-Okay. Thank you.

15:28.135 --> 15:29.845
-[Geun-sik] Enjoy.
-Sir?

15:29.929 --> 15:31.805
We're making a NerTube video. Can we film?

15:31.889 --> 15:33.057
Film?

15:33.140 --> 15:35.017
You've been filming since before.

15:35.100 --> 15:37.728
The atmosphere here is just great.

15:37.811 --> 15:41.482
Vintage and retro places like this
are all the rage these days.

15:41.565 --> 15:42.733
Vintage?

15:42.816 --> 15:43.817
[both chuckling]

15:44.485 --> 15:46.403
Also, our channel has
100,000 subscribers.

15:46.487 --> 15:47.988
It has 100,000 subscribers?

15:48.072 --> 15:48.906
[boy 2] Yes.

15:48.989 --> 15:51.951
Wow, you guys are incredible.

15:52.034 --> 15:54.620
Please, film the food so it looks good!

15:54.703 --> 15:55.788
[boy 1] Okay.

15:55.871 --> 15:57.831
-I'll get you some more.
-No, it's okay!

15:57.915 --> 15:59.124
We have to buy it all!

15:59.208 --> 16:01.377
-Not sponsored?
-[boy 2] That's right.

16:01.460 --> 16:02.836
Okay, I understand.

16:02.920 --> 16:03.796
It can't be fake.

16:03.879 --> 16:05.089
Let's make a thumbnail.

16:07.758 --> 16:10.552
You and Tony know each other?
Why didn't you tell me?

16:10.636 --> 16:13.555
-I'm usually simple and modest.
-[exclaims]

16:13.639 --> 16:16.475
I'm not the type
who mixes business with pleasure!

16:16.558 --> 16:18.018
-[Seok-ryu] I knew it.
-[laughing]

16:18.102 --> 16:18.978
[Seok-ryu] Hey.

16:19.061 --> 16:20.437
[Myeong-u] Did you visit the site?

16:20.521 --> 16:21.355
Yeah.

16:21.438 --> 16:23.482
What are you doing? Why is she here?

16:23.565 --> 16:24.942
I called her.

16:25.567 --> 16:28.278
This is great.
I wanted to talk to you about something.

16:29.029 --> 16:31.281
The thing is…

16:32.241 --> 16:34.368
I wanted to ask Seok-ryu to join

16:34.451 --> 16:36.412
the Greip flagship store project.

16:36.495 --> 16:38.080
-Me?
-[Myeong-u] Yes.

16:38.163 --> 16:41.291
Not now, but it'll start soon.

16:41.375 --> 16:43.460
We got rid of the obstacles too.

16:43.544 --> 16:45.045
How about working with us again?

16:45.129 --> 16:47.214
Look over documents
and join our meetings.

16:47.297 --> 16:49.299
-I'm against it.
-[Myeong-u] What?

16:49.383 --> 16:51.844
We asked for her help
on the new building project.

16:51.927 --> 16:54.054
Our agreement ended
after the presentation.

16:54.847 --> 16:57.975
Asking her help
for the flagship store is unreasonable.

16:58.684 --> 17:00.644
-You think so?
-[Seung-hyo] Of course.

17:00.728 --> 17:03.230
She has plans too.
We can't hold onto her forever.

17:03.856 --> 17:05.566
It's not related with work either.

17:06.233 --> 17:11.280
Also, I don't want to keep having her
involved with her former company.

17:11.363 --> 17:14.491
[Myeong-u] Yeah.
On second thought, you're right.

17:14.575 --> 17:16.243
I was only thinking about us.

17:16.326 --> 17:17.536
I'm really sorry.

17:17.619 --> 17:19.747
You've helped us so much already.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.790
No, it's fine.

17:22.541 --> 17:26.378
It's too bad,
but I guess this is where we part ways.

17:26.462 --> 17:29.173
Still, let's have a farewell party

17:29.256 --> 17:31.383
and go somewhere nice for a meal.

17:31.925 --> 17:33.302
-Sounds good!
-Is that okay?

17:33.385 --> 17:35.387
-[Seok-ryu] Of course.
-[laughing]

17:35.471 --> 17:36.889
Should we invite Na-yun too?

17:36.972 --> 17:38.140
Let's all go together.

17:39.391 --> 17:40.976
Eat as much as you want today.

17:41.060 --> 17:42.936
-I'm paying!
-[Seok-ryu exclaims]

17:43.020 --> 17:44.480
It's the company card anyway.

17:44.563 --> 17:46.482
What a sharp observation.
So sharp it hurts.

17:47.232 --> 17:48.817
Na-yun, take a lot of pictures.

17:48.901 --> 17:50.277
You rarely post these days.

17:50.360 --> 17:51.236
Okay.

17:51.320 --> 17:52.196
[Myeong-u] Thanks.

17:52.279 --> 17:53.655
Seok-ryu, today's guest of honor.

17:53.739 --> 17:54.656
Eat up!

17:54.740 --> 17:56.867
-Thank you.
-[Myeong-u] You're welcome.

17:56.950 --> 17:58.786
[chef] The next dish is salmon roe.

17:58.869 --> 18:02.247
Wow, you don't see this often these days.

18:02.331 --> 18:04.208
Koreans don't really like salmon roe.

18:04.291 --> 18:05.876
Really? I like it.

18:07.044 --> 18:08.253
Me too.

18:08.337 --> 18:11.131
I like everything you like.

18:11.215 --> 18:12.883
She's at it again.

18:12.966 --> 18:15.385
Salmon is so interesting though.

18:15.469 --> 18:17.930
They're born in rivers
and swim down to the ocean.

18:18.013 --> 18:20.933
And they return to the river
to lay their eggs.

18:21.016 --> 18:23.894
[Seok-ryu] You mean their instinct
to return to their origins?

18:23.977 --> 18:26.313
I heard they haven't discovered
why they do that.

18:26.396 --> 18:29.024
Gosh, these animals are stuck in the past.

18:29.108 --> 18:32.361
Right? They went out into the vast world.
Why go to the trouble to return?

18:32.444 --> 18:34.696
What? Did they leave
their first love behind at home?

18:34.780 --> 18:35.656
[laughing]

18:39.993 --> 18:41.620
Why give it to me?
You said you liked it.

18:41.703 --> 18:43.122
I don't like it anymore.

18:43.205 --> 18:45.457
Really? Lucky me.

18:45.541 --> 18:49.753
I'll eat these strong salmon
that swim upstream then.

18:49.837 --> 18:52.172
I heard you like online novels, Na-yun.

18:52.256 --> 18:53.924
Yeah, I don't hate them.

18:54.007 --> 18:54.883
What do you read?

18:54.967 --> 18:57.136
Can you recommend any good ones?

18:57.219 --> 18:59.930
Themes of returning to the past
are popular these days.

19:00.013 --> 19:00.973
[Seok-ryu] Mmm.

19:01.056 --> 19:03.142
[Na-yun] The protagonist
deeply regrets something

19:03.225 --> 19:05.060
and goes back to the past to fix it.

19:05.144 --> 19:08.063
Don't read those.
Why read something so pointless?

19:08.147 --> 19:11.400
People should live
with their eyes on the future.

19:11.483 --> 19:12.776
Why go back to the past?

19:13.443 --> 19:16.196
It's all in the past.
Just forget it, okay?

19:16.697 --> 19:18.407
Live a new and fresh life.

19:20.826 --> 19:21.827
[Seok-ryu clears throat]

19:22.870 --> 19:24.079
When's the next dish?

19:24.163 --> 19:25.330
[chef] It's coming right now.

19:26.456 --> 19:28.125
You totally ruined the mood.

19:28.208 --> 19:29.626
[Myeong-u chuckles nervously]

19:29.710 --> 19:31.628
It's okay.

19:32.546 --> 19:33.380
What's that?

19:33.463 --> 19:34.882
[chef] It's sea bream sushi.

19:38.677 --> 19:40.721
Where's that kid today?

19:40.804 --> 19:42.514
I wanted to ask what her name was today.

19:52.816 --> 19:53.817
Oh?

19:55.777 --> 19:57.487
You should be wary of other people's eyes.

19:57.571 --> 19:58.447
What?

19:58.530 --> 20:00.782
You're showing off
your behind a bit too much.

20:01.450 --> 20:02.659
I'm so sorry.

20:02.743 --> 20:04.453
I was looking for something.

20:04.536 --> 20:05.704
Did you lose something?

20:05.787 --> 20:08.749
No, it's not that.
I'm looking for a four-leaf clover.

20:08.832 --> 20:09.875
What?

20:11.168 --> 20:14.129
Why are you looking
for such an old-fashioned thing?

20:14.213 --> 20:16.381
They even sell those online these days.

20:16.465 --> 20:18.342
It's something classic
that transcends time.

20:18.425 --> 20:19.968
It's the thought that counts.

20:20.052 --> 20:21.136
Can you see thoughts?

20:22.429 --> 20:23.639
You can be on your way.

20:24.431 --> 20:25.807
I was on my way here, okay?

20:27.643 --> 20:29.478
It's not like they easy to find.

20:29.561 --> 20:30.979
[quirky music playing]

20:31.063 --> 20:32.689
Is it for a girl?

20:32.773 --> 20:33.607
Yes.

20:33.690 --> 20:35.984
-I found one!
-What?

20:36.068 --> 20:37.361
It's a normal clover.

20:37.986 --> 20:38.820
[grunts]

20:39.738 --> 20:42.199
[exclaiming]

20:43.742 --> 20:45.786
I found it! I mean it this time!

20:46.370 --> 20:47.246
[Dan-ho sighs]

20:47.329 --> 20:51.375
There are one, two, three, four leaves.

20:51.458 --> 20:52.417
Holy cow.

20:52.501 --> 20:55.837
Really? How did you find it?

20:57.130 --> 20:58.173
Wow…

21:00.968 --> 21:03.095
I concentrate well and have good eyesight.

21:07.891 --> 21:08.850
You can have it.

21:09.434 --> 21:10.519
I don't need it.

21:10.602 --> 21:11.895
-Really?
-Yes.

21:11.979 --> 21:13.772
Thank you. [chuckling]

21:13.855 --> 21:14.690
Thank you! Bye!

21:14.773 --> 21:15.607
[Mo-eum] Bye.

21:16.900 --> 21:19.444
Make sure you laminate it first
before you give it!

21:19.528 --> 21:23.031
Okay? Gosh, I wonder
if he'll even do it properly.

21:23.115 --> 21:25.325
He's so weird.

21:26.910 --> 21:29.246
How can you work right after you eat?

21:29.329 --> 21:31.206
Here, drink this.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.252
I said I was busy.
Why follow me here? Just go home.

21:35.335 --> 21:37.796
I'm leaving after I drink this tea.

21:37.879 --> 21:39.548
It sounds like you're kicking me out.

21:40.424 --> 21:41.258
[slurps]

21:42.634 --> 21:46.179
Hey, you really don't need me
for that project?

21:46.972 --> 21:49.141
I mean, if you're doing it for me,

21:49.224 --> 21:50.559
it's okay.

21:50.642 --> 21:52.269
I can make some time for you.

21:52.352 --> 21:54.062
Are you out of your mind?

21:54.855 --> 21:56.648
-What?
-You said you'd find your dream.

21:57.566 --> 21:59.234
You should be giving it your all,

21:59.318 --> 22:01.194
but you're busy dawdling here and there.

22:01.278 --> 22:02.487
No, it's just…

22:02.571 --> 22:04.990
I'll take care of my own business.

22:05.073 --> 22:06.825
Just focus on your own business.

22:07.451 --> 22:10.287
Don't blame me down the road
when things don't work out.

22:10.370 --> 22:11.371
Hey.

22:12.789 --> 22:14.666
I was trying to be considerate.

22:16.001 --> 22:18.587
-I want to help you--
-I don't need your help.

22:18.670 --> 22:20.130
[Seok-ryu] Fine.

22:20.213 --> 22:22.632
Also, I've been trying hard too.

22:23.300 --> 22:25.761
I think about what my dream
could be more than anyone.

22:25.844 --> 22:27.137
I do it every day.

22:27.220 --> 22:28.138
Really?

22:28.889 --> 22:30.682
Then, don't just think about it and do it.

22:35.270 --> 22:36.271
[Seok-ryu] Hey!

22:36.938 --> 22:38.648
Are you mad at me about something?

22:40.067 --> 22:42.360
Are you venting? Are you holding a grudge?

22:42.861 --> 22:45.572
Is it about losing
Greip's new building because of Chris?

22:46.740 --> 22:48.825
What do you take me for?

22:48.909 --> 22:50.952
[serious music playing]

22:57.542 --> 22:58.835
Hey, honey. It's been a while.

23:05.801 --> 23:08.095
How could you be so shameless
and come here?

23:08.178 --> 23:09.846
Don't you feel bad to face Seung-hyo?

23:10.430 --> 23:11.765
Not at all.

23:11.848 --> 23:13.642
Is it awkward for you to see me?

23:15.685 --> 23:16.561
It's not comfortable.

23:16.645 --> 23:19.481
-It's better if things are uncomfortable.
-[Myeong-u] Jang Tae-hui!

23:20.524 --> 23:23.110
You dumped him for another guy.
Don't play games!

23:23.193 --> 23:25.112
That's a bit harsh.

23:26.029 --> 23:28.198
What will you do if I'm here as a client?

23:32.410 --> 23:33.620
Do you have a request?

23:33.703 --> 23:36.581
I do have a request.

23:37.249 --> 23:38.500
May I ask

23:38.583 --> 23:40.919
why someone of your stature
would pay a visit

23:41.002 --> 23:42.546
to our humble office?

23:44.005 --> 23:45.590
Try to maintain some dignity.

23:45.674 --> 23:46.758
Does dignity pay the bills?

23:46.842 --> 23:48.969
Don't worry about him. Please, go ahead.

23:50.762 --> 23:53.348
Have you two heard of Fresco?

23:53.431 --> 23:55.016
It's an international home decor brand.

23:55.100 --> 23:59.271
Don't they make bowls, kitchen utensils,
pots, and electronic appliances?

23:59.354 --> 24:00.188
That's right.

24:00.272 --> 24:01.523
Fresco collaborates

24:01.606 --> 24:04.484
with world-renowned artists every year
and releases new products.

24:04.568 --> 24:05.569
They're limited editions.

24:05.652 --> 24:08.405
I know.
Dali once collaborated with them too.

24:09.072 --> 24:11.366
I was offered to be part of the project.

24:11.449 --> 24:13.910
What? It has nothing to do with us.

24:13.994 --> 24:16.538
Did you come here to brag
about being a master of onggi?

24:16.621 --> 24:19.749
I'm planning to design
a coffee pot with an onggi concept.

24:20.250 --> 24:22.002
To preserve the structural beauty,

24:22.085 --> 24:24.087
I thought working
with an architect would be good.

24:24.171 --> 24:25.630
That's when I thought of you.

24:26.173 --> 24:28.717
[Myeong-u] What?
And you want to take him from me?

24:28.800 --> 24:30.844
Dream on. He's very busy!

24:30.927 --> 24:33.471
Myeong-u, I didn't get you
a wedding gift, right?

24:33.555 --> 24:34.931
I'll give you a bowl.

24:35.015 --> 24:37.684
A bowl? Like the ones on the news
worth several million won?

24:37.767 --> 24:39.311
-Yeah.
-You can borrow him.

24:39.394 --> 24:41.062
Use him and return him in good condition.

24:41.146 --> 24:42.022
[chuckles softly]

24:42.981 --> 24:45.400
Borrow? What am I, some kind of object?

24:45.483 --> 24:46.651
No, you're a genius.

24:46.735 --> 24:49.321
You can't miss your chance
to be on par with Dali.

24:49.404 --> 24:50.655
We're done talking. Bye.

24:50.739 --> 24:52.574
Wait. Where are you going?

24:52.657 --> 24:54.868
I have to tell Hye-ran
we're getting a bowl.

24:55.577 --> 24:56.995
[laughing]

25:03.543 --> 25:05.712
What are they,
filming Architecture 101 in there?

25:05.795 --> 25:08.423
Why would his ex-girlfriend
come to the office?

25:10.342 --> 25:12.010
Do you know about that woman?

25:12.093 --> 25:13.428
Her name's Jang Tae-hui.

25:13.511 --> 25:17.224
She's a year older, she studied art,
and they met in college.

25:17.307 --> 25:18.850
They dated for over a year.

25:18.934 --> 25:21.937
Come on. I already knew that.

25:22.520 --> 25:25.065
What else? Do you know anything more?

25:25.148 --> 25:26.233
Mmm.

25:27.692 --> 25:30.987
-They had a passionate relationship.
-Passionate?

25:31.071 --> 25:32.822
It was burning hot.

25:33.448 --> 25:34.991
[quirky music playing]

25:39.537 --> 25:40.872
What's this?

25:40.956 --> 25:42.832
Who parked in front of our house?

25:42.916 --> 25:44.125
[gasps]

25:45.585 --> 25:46.586
[kissing]

25:47.212 --> 25:50.340
Wow. Korea's loosened up a lot
since I've been gone.

25:50.423 --> 25:52.050
It's totally liberated now.

25:54.261 --> 25:59.015
Excuse me? It's great that you're in love,
but there's a time and a place for this.

25:59.099 --> 26:01.559
You're right in front of my house.

26:03.186 --> 26:04.062
Excuse me.

26:07.899 --> 26:11.861
Mom, the store was out
of your favorite ice creams.

26:12.445 --> 26:13.822
Who was that?

26:13.905 --> 26:15.573
What? [clears throat]

26:16.533 --> 26:17.367
[music ends]

26:17.450 --> 26:19.202
We looked that passionate?

26:19.703 --> 26:21.663
-Seriously, Seok-ryu?
-[Seok-ryu] Sorry.

26:22.289 --> 26:24.082
Sorry, I shouldn't have said that.

26:24.749 --> 26:26.251
That's okay.

26:26.334 --> 26:28.169
It was a good memory.

26:28.253 --> 26:29.212
[groans softly]

26:29.296 --> 26:30.880
I offer my apologies once more.

26:30.964 --> 26:32.299
I accept.

26:32.382 --> 26:33.842
Did you say your name was Seok-ryu?

26:33.925 --> 26:35.468
Yes, that's right.

26:36.052 --> 26:37.053
It's nice to meet you.

26:37.721 --> 26:40.098
He's told me so much about you.
It's like I know you.

26:40.765 --> 26:42.309
-No, I didn't.
-Yes, you did.

26:44.269 --> 26:46.938
But didn't you live in the US?

26:47.022 --> 26:48.940
I just moved back recently.

26:49.024 --> 26:50.608
I see.

26:50.692 --> 26:53.194
That's great. Can you help me?

26:53.278 --> 26:55.572
What? With what?

26:55.655 --> 26:58.241
I received a great opportunity
and made a proposal,

27:00.201 --> 27:01.745
but he won't take it.

27:02.329 --> 27:05.373
-Can't you convince him as his friend?
-Stop doing as you please.

27:06.041 --> 27:07.709
That's my charm. Did you forget?

27:08.793 --> 27:10.045
You need time to think?

27:10.712 --> 27:11.588
Yeah.

27:11.671 --> 27:14.591
Then, how about coming to my studio?

27:15.133 --> 27:16.426
Take a look and decide.

27:16.509 --> 27:19.054
Really? Are you free this weekend?

27:19.137 --> 27:20.555
[chuckles] Of course.

27:21.723 --> 27:23.391
Bring all of your employees then.

27:24.059 --> 27:25.477
There are plenty of rooms.

27:25.560 --> 27:28.688
Seung-hyo, we'll hold
a company workshop this weekend. Nice!

27:28.772 --> 27:31.399
We're not going. We're busy.

27:31.483 --> 27:34.778
You can't live life
occupied by work all the time.

27:34.861 --> 27:37.614
You should give yourself
time to rest too. Right?

27:37.697 --> 27:39.783
You think I don't know what you're up to?

27:39.866 --> 27:41.868
You're trying to escape
from watching the kids.

27:41.951 --> 27:44.329
They don't sleep.
Help me out this one time.

27:44.412 --> 27:46.206
-Everyone has to come then.
-Okay, thanks.

27:48.541 --> 27:50.627
-You should come too.
-No.

27:50.710 --> 27:53.671
I can't even manage
my own affairs right now.

27:54.255 --> 27:56.216
Also, this is for the employees.

27:56.299 --> 27:58.385
An outsider like me shouldn't join.

27:59.969 --> 28:00.929
[mellow music playing]

28:04.724 --> 28:07.102
That's too bad. It would've been fun.

28:12.649 --> 28:13.650
[phone vibrating]

28:15.985 --> 28:19.030
It was great seeing you.
It made my heart race.

28:21.699 --> 28:22.826
[door opens]

28:25.245 --> 28:26.371
[door closes]

28:28.706 --> 28:29.916
Mr. Bae?

28:31.334 --> 28:32.252
Hey, Seung-hyo.

28:34.421 --> 28:35.422
[chuckles nervously]

28:38.925 --> 28:41.928
Didn't you quit smoking last year?
Is something wrong?

28:42.595 --> 28:44.764
No, it's nothing.

28:45.390 --> 28:47.976
I guess I was feeling restless
without my wife here.

28:48.059 --> 28:49.394
[pop song playing in background]

28:49.477 --> 28:50.979
Hey.

28:51.062 --> 28:52.564
-Are you going to rat me out?
-Maybe.

28:53.231 --> 28:55.150
I didn't see you actually smoke it.

28:55.233 --> 28:56.693
Wow…

28:57.360 --> 29:00.363
My wife raised you properly.

29:04.576 --> 29:05.785
Do you want a drink?

29:05.869 --> 29:06.953
[inhales]

29:08.413 --> 29:11.124
-Just one drink. Sure.
-[chuckles]

29:14.627 --> 29:15.628
-I'll pour it.
-Okay.

29:28.475 --> 29:31.561
[Seok-ryu] Hey, Dong-jin. Wake up!

29:31.644 --> 29:32.937
Wake up!

29:33.938 --> 29:34.898
[footsteps approaching]

29:36.858 --> 29:37.942
Hey, punk.

29:38.026 --> 29:40.695
You should wake up
as soon as the sun rises.

29:40.779 --> 29:44.491
Why are you putting me to work?
Do I have wake you up myself?

29:45.867 --> 29:47.076
I gave you a chance.

29:50.038 --> 29:53.666
Mom said I could beat you up
if you didn't wake up!

29:53.750 --> 29:54.584
Get up!

29:55.752 --> 29:56.628
I said get up!

29:57.295 --> 29:59.589
[man] That's enough!

30:00.757 --> 30:02.050
[pleasant music playing]

30:07.555 --> 30:09.808
What? What are you doing here?

30:11.601 --> 30:13.520
[Dong-jin] Dad!
They're doing something weird!

30:14.020 --> 30:16.022
-Dad!
-Hey! No!

30:16.105 --> 30:17.857
Dong-jin, it's not what you think!

30:18.817 --> 30:20.735
[grunts] Hey, it's a misunderstanding!

30:20.819 --> 30:21.945
[thuds]

30:23.279 --> 30:26.032
Ow…

30:26.991 --> 30:28.076
[yelps]

30:29.410 --> 30:30.870
-[music ends]
-[Seung-hyo groans]

30:34.249 --> 30:35.750
You sprained your toe.

30:35.834 --> 30:38.920
That means it's not broken, right?

30:39.003 --> 30:41.548
That's right. He slightly tore a ligament.

30:41.631 --> 30:44.509
That's not possible. I can't move my foot.

30:44.592 --> 30:47.095
I don't know.
It really shouldn't hurt that much.

30:47.178 --> 30:48.221
[Seok-ryu] Mr. Choi.

30:48.304 --> 30:49.973
He's a bit of a crybaby.

30:50.056 --> 30:51.432
[Seung-hyo] You must've forgotten,

30:51.516 --> 30:53.643
but my leg has been through trauma.

30:53.726 --> 30:56.145
That again?
Are you going to milk that forever?

30:56.229 --> 30:57.397
Milking…

30:57.480 --> 30:58.606
You're being harsh.

30:58.690 --> 31:02.026
Goodness, I am so sorry.

31:02.110 --> 31:05.488
But is your toe the same as your leg?

31:06.239 --> 31:09.409
Hey, toes are a part of the leg.

31:09.492 --> 31:10.410
It's all one limb.

31:10.493 --> 31:13.288
Yeah, I see.

31:13.371 --> 31:16.165
So that means your toenail
is a part of your leg too.

31:17.208 --> 31:19.085
How's Seung-hyo? Is he okay?

31:19.168 --> 31:22.881
Yeah, he needs a cast for week
and medication for three days.

31:22.964 --> 31:24.173
That's good.

31:24.257 --> 31:26.718
Why did you beat him up like that?

31:26.801 --> 31:28.928
He didn't get hurt from that!

31:29.012 --> 31:31.681
He tripped over his own feet and fell.

31:31.764 --> 31:33.224
[Geun-sik] Because you hit him.

31:33.308 --> 31:35.727
Let's check it again
if it still hurts in a week.

31:36.311 --> 31:37.145
Okay.

31:39.647 --> 31:41.190
How did this happen though?

31:42.567 --> 31:44.652
Well…

31:44.736 --> 31:45.737
[quirky music playing]

31:45.820 --> 31:50.074
[drunkenly] I wanted to pay,
but I forgot my wallet. [chuckles]

31:50.658 --> 31:52.785
You can treat me next time.

31:52.869 --> 31:54.954
Okay, where are we going now?

31:55.038 --> 31:57.790
-Where's round two? Your house?
-Round two?

31:57.874 --> 31:58.958
How about my house?

31:59.042 --> 32:01.085
No, Mrs. Na would kill us.

32:01.169 --> 32:05.590
Hey! Listen, you brat!
I'm the man of the house!

32:05.673 --> 32:07.133
My wife's not home right now.

32:07.216 --> 32:08.635
[laughing]

32:08.718 --> 32:10.929
Right, she's not home.
My mom's not here either.

32:12.388 --> 32:13.348
She's not home!

32:13.431 --> 32:16.059
Wow! She's not home! I love it!

32:16.142 --> 32:19.938
I'm free! I'm a free man!

32:20.021 --> 32:21.230
Eat this.

32:21.314 --> 32:22.357
Hey.

32:22.440 --> 32:27.737
We'll have drinks at my house,
and you can sleep in Dong-jin's room.

32:27.820 --> 32:29.489
-Okay? Not Seok-ryu's room.
-Okay.

32:29.572 --> 32:31.658
-Sleep in Dong-jin's room. Got it?
-Okay.

32:31.741 --> 32:32.575
Okay.

32:32.659 --> 32:37.288
We'll go to my house, and I'll take out

32:37.372 --> 32:42.293
my wild ginseng wine for you.

32:42.377 --> 32:44.420
Come on, wild ginseng wine?

32:44.504 --> 32:46.881
You sure it's not regular or red ginseng?

32:46.965 --> 32:51.094
Hey! It's real wild ginseng wine!

32:51.177 --> 32:52.887
It's the real deal, okay?

32:54.180 --> 32:55.348
Then…

32:55.932 --> 32:59.519
-Sound good? Let's go to my house!
-Yeah. [chuckling]

32:59.602 --> 33:01.813
Let's go to Seok-ryu's house!

33:01.896 --> 33:04.524
[in normal voice] You're like your mom.
You're so violent.

33:05.233 --> 33:06.067
Let go.

33:09.529 --> 33:12.156
Don't drink with him.

33:12.240 --> 33:14.534
He has terrible habits when he's drunk.

33:16.452 --> 33:17.286
[music ends]

33:17.370 --> 33:19.998
-I'm sorry. I should be driving you home.
-It's fine.

33:20.081 --> 33:23.751
-But I have to go to my workshop.
-Forget it. I can take the bus.

33:23.835 --> 33:24.919
Are you really okay?

33:25.003 --> 33:26.796
-I'm fine.
-Okay.

33:26.879 --> 33:27.755
Hey, let's go.

33:28.339 --> 33:31.092
I have plans. Go ahead, Dad.

33:31.175 --> 33:32.301
All of a sudden?

33:32.969 --> 33:35.972
I guess I'm going alone.
Don't come home so late.

33:36.055 --> 33:38.683
-It's scary at night.
-Okay.

33:38.766 --> 33:39.600
What a nag.

33:39.684 --> 33:41.144
-Bye.
-Take care, sir.

33:41.227 --> 33:42.311
Bye, Dad.

33:47.734 --> 33:50.987
-Hey. What are you doing?
-Why act so surprised?

33:51.654 --> 33:53.281
I drove your car here.

33:53.948 --> 33:55.283
-So what?
-I mean…

33:56.117 --> 33:58.995
I may not have
directly caused your injury,

33:59.078 --> 34:01.330
but I do bear
some indirect responsibility.

34:01.414 --> 34:03.624
I'll take care of you
until your cast comes off.

34:03.708 --> 34:05.126
Why would you do that?

34:06.836 --> 34:08.504
-Give me the keys.
-You want them?

34:08.588 --> 34:11.966
Sure, drive yourself then.

34:12.050 --> 34:12.884
Here.

34:13.468 --> 34:14.385
[groans softly]

34:17.221 --> 34:18.139
[exclaims in pain]

34:18.765 --> 34:20.224
[quirky music playing]

34:20.308 --> 34:21.642
Hey, Seok-ryu?

34:23.144 --> 34:24.145
[Seok-ryu] Yeah?

34:25.730 --> 34:26.731
[keys jingling]

34:27.231 --> 34:28.316
What?

34:28.900 --> 34:29.901
This…

34:30.610 --> 34:31.903
[Seok-ryu] What do you want?

34:33.905 --> 34:36.407
It's Saturday. Where are you going?

34:36.491 --> 34:38.743
The convenience store.
Then, I'm off to work.

34:38.826 --> 34:41.662
I've already stopped by,
and I'm on my way to cover a story.

34:41.746 --> 34:44.290
Wow, I didn't ask. Good luck.

34:44.373 --> 34:46.667
Ms. Paramedic, wait.

34:47.835 --> 34:49.212
You'll be looking for this.

34:51.214 --> 34:52.423
[pleasant music playing]

34:52.507 --> 34:54.801
It's for helping me find
the four-leaf clover.

34:54.884 --> 34:56.511
Oh.

34:56.594 --> 34:58.846
But aren't these yours?

34:59.889 --> 35:00.807
I bought two.

35:00.890 --> 35:01.724
[chuckles softly]

35:02.266 --> 35:04.435
If that's the case, thank you.

35:05.228 --> 35:07.730
But did that person
like the four-leaf clover?

35:07.814 --> 35:09.565
No, she didn't.

35:10.525 --> 35:13.361
I said I tried hard
and another woman helped me find it--

35:13.444 --> 35:14.278
What?

35:14.987 --> 35:16.447
Why would you tell her that?

35:17.198 --> 35:20.076
"I searched on my own for a long time."
You should've said that.

35:20.660 --> 35:22.286
I can't lie.

35:22.370 --> 35:24.622
-[Mo-eum] Oh.
-I'll get going now.

35:26.207 --> 35:27.208
Why…

35:29.836 --> 35:30.962
[sighs]

35:31.879 --> 35:34.382
Gosh, he knows nothing about women at all.

35:38.302 --> 35:41.556
Mr. Kang, let's take a short break.
What do you say?

35:41.639 --> 35:42.807
We can't.

35:42.890 --> 35:45.226
We volunteered
so that elderly lady could rest.

35:45.309 --> 35:46.936
We have to pick up as many as we can.

35:47.019 --> 35:50.398
Hey, you asked me for help
to write a special feature.

35:50.481 --> 35:52.692
This is no way
to treat your older colleague.

35:52.775 --> 35:55.987
Now that you're out in the field
after being stuck at your desk,

35:56.070 --> 35:57.864
doesn't it feel like you're alive?

35:58.614 --> 36:00.867
I'm on the verge of death, you punk!

36:01.701 --> 36:05.621
I'm disappointed.
You weren't like this in the past.

36:05.705 --> 36:08.916
Hey, are you getting revenge
for what I said to you before?

36:09.000 --> 36:10.418
Of course not.

36:10.501 --> 36:12.712
Okay, boosters on!

36:12.795 --> 36:14.755
[Yeong-in] Hey, slow down!

36:14.839 --> 36:16.132
-[Dan-ho] Go.
-[Yeong-in screams]

36:16.215 --> 36:18.217
I can't do this! Jeez!

36:18.301 --> 36:20.344
-Hey!
-[Dan-ho] Are you going to help or not?

36:31.063 --> 36:32.023
[Seung-hyo exhales]

36:32.106 --> 36:33.149
Why are you scared?

36:33.232 --> 36:37.028
Look, I was the best driver in the US.

36:37.612 --> 36:40.198
Hey, don't turn your head. Watch the road.

36:40.781 --> 36:42.241
And stick to the speed limit.

36:43.159 --> 36:44.285
[presses button]

36:44.869 --> 36:46.537
Stop pressing random buttons.

36:46.621 --> 36:48.080
[breathes deeply]

36:49.123 --> 36:50.583
Don't touch anything.

36:50.666 --> 36:52.376
[pop song playing over stereo]

36:54.629 --> 36:57.048
Hey! Come on.

36:57.632 --> 37:01.719
The breeze, music, and relaxation.
Isn't this just perfect?

37:01.802 --> 37:04.472
-Hey!
-[Seok-ryu] This is nice.

37:05.348 --> 37:09.477
Sir, just enjoy the relaxing ride. Okay?

37:13.105 --> 37:13.940
[sighs]

37:28.496 --> 37:29.330
[song ends]

37:34.543 --> 37:35.419
[groans]

37:35.503 --> 37:37.129
Relaxing, my foot.

37:37.213 --> 37:38.965
Who drives like that?

37:39.840 --> 37:41.259
Hey!

37:41.342 --> 37:42.802
-[Seung-hyo] Hi.
-[car door closes]

37:43.302 --> 37:44.387
What happened to your foot?

37:45.221 --> 37:46.055
Ask her.

37:46.722 --> 37:49.016
[Seok-ryu] Hello. He got hurt a little.

37:49.100 --> 37:51.686
Not a lot though.
He'll need two weeks to recover.

37:51.769 --> 37:54.438
So I had no choice but to come too.

37:54.522 --> 37:56.482
I see.

37:56.565 --> 37:57.858
I'm glad you're here.

37:57.942 --> 38:00.152
Myeong-u's going to be late.
Did you get his call?

38:00.236 --> 38:01.237
No.

38:02.738 --> 38:04.115
When did all these calls come in?

38:04.198 --> 38:06.909
He has an upset stomach.
I think it's pretty bad.

38:06.993 --> 38:09.120
Jeez, what did he eat this time?

38:10.538 --> 38:11.914
[Tae-hui] Let's go inside.

38:11.998 --> 38:13.457
[quirky music playing]

38:14.500 --> 38:16.335
What? I can't help you walk?

38:16.419 --> 38:17.712
No, it's fine.

38:18.254 --> 38:19.088
[clears throat]

38:20.256 --> 38:21.507
-Come on.
-Sure.

38:30.391 --> 38:31.392
[Seung-hyo] Wow.

38:33.686 --> 38:34.645
[Seok-ryu] Wow!

38:36.147 --> 38:37.982
Did you make all of those, Tae-hui?

38:39.650 --> 38:43.154
Is it okay if I call you that?

38:43.738 --> 38:44.655
Of course.

38:44.739 --> 38:47.867
Tae-hui, can I go see them up close?

38:47.950 --> 38:48.826
Sure.

38:52.163 --> 38:53.164
[chuckles softly]

38:54.790 --> 38:57.251
She's cute. She's like a puppy.

38:59.086 --> 39:01.881
If you're talking about Seok-ryu,
that's not the right description.

39:01.964 --> 39:02.798
Why not?

39:03.549 --> 39:05.801
Are you jealous
because I called someone else cute?

39:06.719 --> 39:07.595
There you go again.

39:07.678 --> 39:08.888
[chuckles softly]

39:10.931 --> 39:12.558
-Seok-ryu.
-[Seok-ryu] Yes?

39:12.641 --> 39:15.019
[Tae-hui] Don't you want to know
what's inside those jars?

39:15.102 --> 39:16.354
I do!

39:18.147 --> 39:19.565
[gasps] It's meju.

39:19.648 --> 39:21.400
There are so many of them!

39:21.484 --> 39:22.902
[Seung-hyo] Why do you have these?

39:23.569 --> 39:25.363
Don't you make onggi?

39:25.446 --> 39:26.447
I do.

39:27.406 --> 39:30.242
I make sauces and pastes too.

39:30.326 --> 39:31.160
[Seung-hyo] What?

39:32.536 --> 39:35.247
My dad's an expert in food.
He's a doenjang master.

39:35.331 --> 39:36.457
Did you forget?

39:36.540 --> 39:38.834
Yeah, that's right. Sorry.

39:38.918 --> 39:41.879
So does he make it here?

39:41.962 --> 39:44.256
No, he lives in Gangwon Province.

39:44.340 --> 39:46.092
I'm just in charge of this place.

39:46.842 --> 39:48.552
To make good bowls,

39:48.636 --> 39:52.390
I had to learn about the essence
of what went inside them first.

39:52.473 --> 39:56.143
I can sell more onggi if the process
of making sauces and pastes flourish.

39:56.227 --> 39:57.937
It's all part of my big plan.

39:58.020 --> 40:00.022
Do you make the sauces
and pastes yourself?

40:00.106 --> 40:02.441
Yes, with the other ladies
in the neighborhood.

40:02.525 --> 40:04.151
Today happens to be the day for it.

40:05.027 --> 40:07.738
-And I need a few helping hands.
-[Seung-hyo sighs]

40:08.322 --> 40:09.990
Was this your plan all along?

40:10.074 --> 40:12.410
I just wanted to kill
two birds with one stone.

40:12.868 --> 40:13.786
You know I'm greedy.

40:13.869 --> 40:15.788
Still, you can't spring this on us.

40:15.871 --> 40:16.789
I can't help.

40:16.872 --> 40:19.291
I don't think
you could've helped anyway with your foot.

40:19.375 --> 40:21.127
It's not just me. We all can't.

40:21.210 --> 40:23.879
[Seok-ryu] Me! I want to help.

40:23.963 --> 40:26.215
I'll do it! I want to try
and make doenjang!

40:26.298 --> 40:27.174
What?

40:27.258 --> 40:28.843
Why not? I want to do it!

40:29.635 --> 40:31.470
-[Tae-hui] Nice!
-[chuckles]

40:31.554 --> 40:32.805
This is going to be fun!

40:33.681 --> 40:34.890
[pleasant music playing]

40:41.647 --> 40:43.023
[sizzling]

40:48.696 --> 40:49.530
[water splashing]

40:57.371 --> 40:59.165
-How's the work?
-Good.

40:59.707 --> 41:00.708
It's so interesting!

41:01.417 --> 41:02.751
[old lady] Hey, young man.

41:02.835 --> 41:04.795
-[Seung-hyo] Yes?
-Come and help me.

41:05.921 --> 41:07.548
-Open this.
-Okay.

41:07.631 --> 41:09.091
[old lady] Take out the charcoal.

41:09.175 --> 41:11.343
Use that and wipe the inside clean.

41:11.427 --> 41:12.428
Yes, ma'am.

41:16.390 --> 41:17.224
Wow…

41:18.476 --> 41:19.351
[groans]

41:23.647 --> 41:24.565
Thank you.

41:36.494 --> 41:37.953
I have a question.

41:38.037 --> 41:40.915
What are these marks on the meju?

41:40.998 --> 41:42.750
They're from being tied with straw.

41:43.417 --> 41:45.211
They were hung from the ceiling.

41:45.878 --> 41:48.547
I see. So that's why.

41:49.507 --> 41:51.008
What will we do next?

41:51.091 --> 41:52.718
What do you think?

41:52.801 --> 41:55.971
We have to put the doenjang
in the onggis we sterilized earlier.

41:56.055 --> 41:57.681
How do we do that?

41:57.765 --> 41:58.599
[laughs]

41:58.682 --> 42:01.310
You're just full of curiosity, aren't you?

42:01.393 --> 42:03.854
-[laughing]
-That's just how I am.

42:03.938 --> 42:06.398
Why are you in such a hurry?
Take your time to learn.

42:06.482 --> 42:07.775
Yes, ma'am.

42:08.817 --> 42:11.153
She's having a blast.
The time of her life.

42:14.156 --> 42:15.449
Can we talk for a second?

42:16.951 --> 42:18.035
Right now?

42:18.118 --> 42:18.994
[Tae-hui] Yeah.

42:19.078 --> 42:20.454
There's something you need to do.

42:26.710 --> 42:28.003
What do you need my help with?

42:29.630 --> 42:32.508
Just stay here with me for a moment.

42:33.384 --> 42:34.385
[exhales]

42:34.468 --> 42:36.512
-Is this why you called me away?
-[Tae-hui] Yeah.

42:37.304 --> 42:39.723
What? You liked it
when I used to do this.

42:40.474 --> 42:41.559
That was then.

42:43.269 --> 42:44.770
Did you date anyone else after me?

42:44.853 --> 42:46.689
Of course. We broke up a long time ago.

42:47.356 --> 42:48.649
True.

42:48.732 --> 42:51.777
You let people in,
but you also let people out.

42:52.570 --> 42:54.405
We started dating because I asked you out.

42:54.488 --> 42:56.365
If that's how you feel, I'm a little hurt.

42:58.450 --> 43:00.744
I liked you a lot.

43:00.828 --> 43:01.912
Me too.

43:02.955 --> 43:05.040
And I've missed you.

43:07.334 --> 43:10.254
Didn't you come back
just to collaborate on work?

43:10.337 --> 43:13.924
I was genuine
about wanting to work with you.

43:15.009 --> 43:18.345
But using that as an excuse
to see you is also genuine.

43:19.638 --> 43:21.557
I was hoping for serendipity

43:22.141 --> 43:24.476
and that our reunion
could be an opportunity.

43:25.519 --> 43:26.520
It's true.

43:29.523 --> 43:31.442
But work comes first.

43:32.151 --> 43:34.945
This is my collection
that was exhibited in Vienna.

43:39.283 --> 43:40.284
It's nice.

43:41.035 --> 43:43.370
The curves look like columns with entasis.

43:43.454 --> 43:46.457
As expected from an architect.

43:46.540 --> 43:47.875
[chuckles softly]

43:47.958 --> 43:50.085
Want to try making one yourself?

43:59.970 --> 44:01.096
[water splashing]

44:01.180 --> 44:03.932
By the way,
what are the cloth and strainer for?

44:04.016 --> 44:05.392
This will keep debris

44:05.476 --> 44:07.853
-from getting inside.
-[Seok-ryu] Mmm.

44:07.936 --> 44:09.980
[old lady] We're almost done.

44:10.939 --> 44:14.777
You came all the way from Seoul
and had to do so much work.

44:14.860 --> 44:17.488
No, I'm having so much fun.

44:17.571 --> 44:18.530
[all laughing]

44:19.198 --> 44:22.242
You can speak in our dialect pretty well.

44:22.326 --> 44:24.620
-I do?
-[all laughing]

44:24.703 --> 44:26.914
By the way, where's the bathroom?

44:26.997 --> 44:27.831
I have to go.

44:27.915 --> 44:29.333
It's over here.

44:29.416 --> 44:31.085
-I'll be right back.
-Okay.

44:48.102 --> 44:49.478
[mellow music playing]

45:03.867 --> 45:06.286
[Tae-hui] Your hands should go like this.

45:21.844 --> 45:22.845
[chuckles nervously]

45:23.554 --> 45:24.430
You'll ruin it.

45:26.181 --> 45:29.435
I was just looking for the bathroom.

45:29.518 --> 45:31.270
It's at the end of the hall.

45:31.353 --> 45:34.648
[Seok-ryu] Okay.
I'll go now since nature's calling.

45:34.731 --> 45:36.108
I'm sorry I interrupted.

45:40.195 --> 45:41.113
[exhales]

45:44.199 --> 45:45.701
Damn it.

45:54.460 --> 45:55.294
[clears throat]

45:57.629 --> 45:59.089
Hey, sorry about that.

45:59.173 --> 46:01.842
I didn't mean to
cluelessly run into the chair.

46:01.925 --> 46:03.135
What are you talking about?

46:04.303 --> 46:07.097
You two look good together.
It was like a scene from Ghost.

46:07.181 --> 46:08.015
[sighs]

46:08.098 --> 46:10.517
Haven't you heard of it?
Demi Moore's in it.

46:10.601 --> 46:13.604
There's a scene in the movie
with really romantic music.

46:13.687 --> 46:15.230
As she makes pottery, he comes up and…

46:15.314 --> 46:17.107
What are you trying to say?

46:17.191 --> 46:20.360
I'm just saying
I hope things work out for you two.

46:23.405 --> 46:24.865
You never know.

46:24.948 --> 46:27.784
Old feelings could resurface
now that you've met again.

46:29.786 --> 46:32.289
What? Why are you looking at me like that?

46:32.372 --> 46:33.457
I'm warning you.

46:34.416 --> 46:37.461
-Don't meddle in other people's affairs.
-No, I meant…

46:37.544 --> 46:39.630
I only meant it if you still liked her.

46:39.713 --> 46:43.926
-Also, friends can talk about this stuff.
-No, we can't.

46:48.555 --> 46:49.806
[Seok-ryu] Jeez, that little…

46:58.941 --> 47:00.275
[both] Mr. Choi!

47:00.359 --> 47:01.818
Seung-hyo! [groans]

47:01.902 --> 47:03.862
[Na-yun] Seung-hyo,
what's wrong with your leg?

47:03.946 --> 47:05.906
I just bumped into something.

47:05.989 --> 47:07.324
Are you okay?

47:07.407 --> 47:10.786
Seung-hyo, I had such a hard time.
I was in danger multiple times.

47:10.869 --> 47:13.205
We stopped at every rest area
on our way here.

47:13.288 --> 47:14.790
I told you to wear a diaper.

47:14.873 --> 47:17.626
Not putting it on
was my last bit of pride. [stomach growls]

47:17.709 --> 47:19.670
It must've been tough. Go on in.

47:19.753 --> 47:21.255
Where are you going? Your leg's hurt.

47:21.338 --> 47:23.465
I need to get some air.

47:23.549 --> 47:24.550
[Myeong-u] What?

47:27.678 --> 47:30.013
[stomach growls] I'm going inside.
[groans]

47:31.890 --> 47:33.642
[sizzling]

47:34.643 --> 47:36.687
Tae-hui! We're here… What?

47:36.770 --> 47:38.647
-[Tae-hui] You're late.
-[Seok-ryu] Hello!

47:38.730 --> 47:40.566
[Myeong-u] Yeah, but what's all of this?

47:40.649 --> 47:42.818
You said you couldn't make it, Seok-ryu!

47:42.901 --> 47:44.403
It just sort of happened.

47:44.486 --> 47:48.490
Is this a folk village? Is this where you
participate in traditional tasks?

47:48.574 --> 47:49.908
Kind of.

47:49.992 --> 47:52.244
Ma'am, more workers have arrived.

47:52.869 --> 47:55.038
Should we check the pastes
we fermented last time?

47:55.122 --> 47:56.748
Sounds good. [chuckles]

47:56.832 --> 47:58.250
Do what?

47:58.333 --> 47:59.626
So what happens is

47:59.710 --> 48:03.630
they take out the meju and use them
to make deonjang and soy sauce.

48:03.714 --> 48:05.257
-Sounds fun, right?
-[Myeong-u] I see.

48:05.340 --> 48:06.592
[all exclaiming]

48:07.175 --> 48:09.052
-You'll help, right?
-[Myeong-u] Yeah.

48:09.761 --> 48:11.555
Is she insane?

48:11.638 --> 48:14.766
That punk, Seung-hyo.
That's why he acted serious and ran away.

48:15.601 --> 48:16.560
-Seok-ryu?
-Yes?

48:16.643 --> 48:18.103
Where's the bathroom?

48:18.186 --> 48:20.647
-Go around that way.
-[Myeong-u] Okay.

48:20.731 --> 48:22.858
-Go inside the building.
-[Myeong-u] Okay!

48:26.570 --> 48:27.613
[chuckles softly]

48:27.696 --> 48:29.531
-[birds chirping]
-[wind blowing]

48:32.034 --> 48:33.368
[mellow music playing]

48:36.413 --> 48:37.247
[exhales]

48:38.582 --> 48:39.958
-[door closes]
-[exhales]

48:40.834 --> 48:41.960
I left my wallet.

48:42.044 --> 48:45.589
[Mo-eum] Are you okay now? Have you…

48:46.256 --> 48:47.841
completely moved on from him?

48:47.924 --> 48:48.884
[Seok-ryu] No.

48:49.718 --> 48:50.802
I still love him.

49:03.607 --> 49:06.443
Gosh, I left my wallet.

49:06.526 --> 49:07.861
I had to come all the way back.

49:08.570 --> 49:10.864
Hey, you're all okay with beer, right?

49:10.947 --> 49:12.449
No, I want soju tonight.

49:12.532 --> 49:13.909
I want to get drunk.

49:13.992 --> 49:16.203
-Okay. Got it.
-I want non-alcoholic beer.

49:16.286 --> 49:18.288
-And juice.
-[Mo-eum] What?

49:18.372 --> 49:19.581
Why?

49:20.999 --> 49:23.210
No, you're right. Don't get drunk tonight.

49:23.293 --> 49:24.211
That'll be safer.

49:24.294 --> 49:26.588
[Seung-hyo] Don't eat until I get back.
Wait for me.

49:26.672 --> 49:28.090
Don't you dare lay a finger.

49:41.895 --> 49:42.771
[music fades]

49:43.939 --> 49:46.191
-Great job, everyone.
-[Min-ho groans]

49:46.274 --> 49:47.651
Great job.

49:48.568 --> 49:50.112
What time is it?

49:50.195 --> 49:53.031
It's past 3:00 p.m.
We haven't even had lunch yet.

49:53.115 --> 49:55.117
-Should we order something?
-How about Chinese?

49:55.200 --> 49:58.662
Okay, then let's all have fried rice.

49:58.745 --> 49:59.830
I put the order in.

49:59.913 --> 50:01.665
-[emergency alert playing]
-[groans]

50:02.332 --> 50:05.836
[sighs wearily] This is why
we can't order any noodles.

50:06.420 --> 50:07.838
[grunts] Let's go.

50:07.921 --> 50:08.922
[car starts]

50:13.218 --> 50:14.344
[siren blaring]

50:15.637 --> 50:16.513
[paper rustling]

50:23.145 --> 50:24.354
What is it?

50:24.438 --> 50:25.814
[Jeong-u] Nothing.

50:29.234 --> 50:31.570
[Mo-eum] We're emergency responders.
Is anyone home?

50:31.653 --> 50:32.779
[knock on door]

50:32.863 --> 50:34.197
We're coming in.

50:37.868 --> 50:40.287
Is anyone home?

50:41.079 --> 50:43.498
We're paramedics.

50:43.582 --> 50:44.583
What?

50:45.250 --> 50:48.044
Hey, kid!

50:48.128 --> 50:49.629
Hey, wake up!

50:50.213 --> 50:51.339
Hey, kid!

50:51.423 --> 50:52.674
[melancholy music playing]

50:52.758 --> 50:54.718
-[girl mumbling]
-[Mo-eum] Hey.

50:57.262 --> 50:58.263
[sighs in relief]

50:58.346 --> 51:01.224
Hey, kid. Are you okay?

51:01.850 --> 51:03.477
Do you recognize me?

51:05.228 --> 51:07.522
[exhales]

51:08.106 --> 51:09.441
[weakly] It hurts.

51:10.734 --> 51:14.821
I called for help.

51:14.905 --> 51:16.990
[in normal voice]
Good job. You did great.

51:17.073 --> 51:19.159
-[exhales] Great job, kid.
-[girl groans weakly]

51:20.827 --> 51:22.996
[weakly] I'm not a kid.

51:24.039 --> 51:25.123
Yeon-du.

51:26.124 --> 51:27.667
My name…

51:28.835 --> 51:30.712
is Yeon-du.

51:30.796 --> 51:33.006
[in normal voice] Okay, Yeon-du. Good job.

51:33.089 --> 51:35.717
I'll make sure you feel better real quick.
Just wait.

51:36.384 --> 51:37.469
Thank you.

51:38.303 --> 51:40.680
-Do you know her?
-[Min-ho] Where's her guardian?

51:41.890 --> 51:43.350
Was she home alone?

51:43.892 --> 51:45.811
[device beeping]

51:47.687 --> 51:48.522
[Mo-eum exclaiming]

51:53.151 --> 51:55.487
Yeon-du, wake up.

51:55.570 --> 51:56.404
Yeon-du!

51:57.364 --> 51:58.490
Stay with me, Yeon-du!

52:01.618 --> 52:02.452
[groans softly]

52:08.291 --> 52:10.669
Excuse me.
Could someone give me a hand?

52:10.752 --> 52:11.628
I'll help!

52:13.547 --> 52:14.714
What is it?

52:14.798 --> 52:18.969
Well, I think too much sunlight
has dried out the paste.

52:19.052 --> 52:20.512
I want to move it to the studio.

52:21.179 --> 52:23.431
-I'll move it.
-No way.

52:23.515 --> 52:25.016
The jar weighs over 30 kilograms.

52:25.100 --> 52:27.727
-I'll ask the men to do it.
-No, I'm really strong!

52:27.811 --> 52:30.313
-Leave it to me.
-No… Myeong-u?

52:31.147 --> 52:32.649
-Then…
-[Seok-ryu] No, I'll do it.

52:32.732 --> 52:35.944
-[Myeong-u] I'll hold down the fort here.
-He's busy. I'll go.

52:36.027 --> 52:38.071
-We'll be back.
-[Myeong-u] Don't hurt yourself.

52:41.074 --> 52:41.950
[Seok-ryu groans]

52:43.034 --> 52:44.870
This is too difficult for us.

52:44.953 --> 52:46.872
Let's leave it here and call someone.

52:46.955 --> 52:49.374
We're almost there. I'll do it. It's okay.

52:49.457 --> 52:50.917
No, it's too hard.

52:51.001 --> 52:52.210
I'll get someone.

52:52.878 --> 52:54.504
I can do it on my own.

52:57.757 --> 52:58.592
[grunts]

53:01.970 --> 53:03.013
[groans]

53:03.096 --> 53:05.557
-Seok-ryu!
-Bae Seok-ryu!

53:07.058 --> 53:08.268
[Tae-hui] Seok-ryu.

53:08.351 --> 53:09.769
Are you hurt?

53:11.104 --> 53:13.648
-My gosh, the jar and paste!
-Are you okay?

53:13.732 --> 53:16.276
Who cares about me? What about this?

53:16.359 --> 53:17.736
This took so much effort to make!

53:17.819 --> 53:18.987
That's not important.

53:19.070 --> 53:20.989
Why can't you be more careful?

53:21.072 --> 53:23.491
Why get involved when you can't even
take care of yourself?

53:23.575 --> 53:24.409
It's not like that.

53:25.076 --> 53:26.578
She was trying to help me.

53:26.661 --> 53:28.038
I'm sorry. I'll clean it up.

53:28.121 --> 53:29.915
Don't touch it. Don't cause trouble again.

53:31.124 --> 53:32.334
[Tae-hui] That's enough.

53:32.417 --> 53:33.919
She's already startled.

53:34.544 --> 53:36.796
Seok-ryu, I have extra clothes in my room.

53:37.380 --> 53:38.673
-Go and change.
-Okay.

53:39.257 --> 53:41.259
[Tae-hui] The stain won't come out
if it sets.

53:55.357 --> 53:56.191
[sighs]

54:02.656 --> 54:03.865
That jerk.

54:03.949 --> 54:06.576
How could he get so angry at me?
That was so embarrassing.

54:09.245 --> 54:10.246
[door creaking]

54:13.541 --> 54:15.210
[dogs barking in distance]

54:24.761 --> 54:26.471
[old lady] This is my home.

54:26.554 --> 54:28.264
This is how I live.

54:28.348 --> 54:29.891
You're here as guests,

54:29.975 --> 54:32.143
but I'm afraid I can't ask you to come in.

54:32.227 --> 54:33.311
It's too small here.

54:34.437 --> 54:36.147
There's no place to sit.

54:36.231 --> 54:38.692
That's okay. Our legs are strong.

54:38.775 --> 54:42.779
Yes, we're just grateful
to have been invited.

54:42.862 --> 54:45.323
I'm the grateful one.

54:46.116 --> 54:47.575
Reporters like you

54:47.659 --> 54:50.537
came all this way to see someone
as insignificant as me.

54:51.454 --> 54:53.540
And that cart too.

54:54.666 --> 54:56.710
Can I really accept that for free?

54:56.793 --> 54:58.545
I bet it was expensive.

54:59.587 --> 55:00.839
Don't worry.

55:01.548 --> 55:04.217
I processed the expenses
at my manager's discretion.

55:04.300 --> 55:05.760
Stop it. [chuckles softly]

55:06.344 --> 55:10.056
Ma'am, always be careful
of the roads. Okay?

55:10.140 --> 55:12.559
Okay, thank you.

55:13.184 --> 55:16.688
The world has become harsh and unsettling.

55:17.647 --> 55:19.566
But there are still good people.

55:19.649 --> 55:20.817
[Yeong-in chuckles softly]

55:20.900 --> 55:23.111
-Take care of yourself.
-[old lady] Okay.

55:23.695 --> 55:25.363
-Thank you.
-[phone vibrating]

55:29.367 --> 55:30.285
Hello?

55:32.954 --> 55:33.788
What?

55:34.622 --> 55:35.498
Yeon-du?

55:35.582 --> 55:37.417
-Dan-ho!
-[Dan-ho] What do you mean?

55:37.500 --> 55:38.793
Yeon-du's gone?

55:38.877 --> 55:42.338
Yeon-du had a cold.

55:42.422 --> 55:44.841
She was asleep after taking medicine
for her fever at lunch.

55:45.425 --> 55:47.552
I left for a second
to buy groceries and…

55:47.635 --> 55:49.095
So where is she?

55:49.179 --> 55:51.556
I was surprised too.
I asked everyone in the neighborhood.

55:52.307 --> 55:54.309
They said the paramedics came.

55:54.392 --> 55:55.685
[breathing heavily]

55:55.769 --> 55:57.062
[lady sobbing]

55:57.145 --> 55:58.021
[siren blaring]

56:04.652 --> 56:05.737
[Mo-eum] Go slow.

56:11.284 --> 56:12.702
The patient's a five-year-old girl.

56:12.786 --> 56:14.871
Her BP's 100 over 70,
and her heart rate's 120.

56:14.954 --> 56:17.999
She has a fever of 39.6 degrees.
Oxygen saturation is 99%.

56:18.083 --> 56:20.710
She was conscious and responsive
when we arrived,

56:20.794 --> 56:22.712
but she began to decline
and lost consciousness.

56:22.796 --> 56:24.172
Pre-existing conditions or meds?

56:24.255 --> 56:26.716
Her guardian's not here,
so we couldn't check.

56:27.300 --> 56:29.094
Let's give her IV fluids and run tests.

56:29.177 --> 56:30.011
[Mo-eum] Okay.

56:38.937 --> 56:40.271
Just a moment.

56:40.355 --> 56:41.981
[pleasant music playing]

56:47.779 --> 56:49.656
[Dan-ho] Is there a patient
named Kang Yeon-du?

56:49.739 --> 56:51.449
She's a five-year-old girl!

56:51.533 --> 56:52.951
She's over there.

56:58.456 --> 56:59.290
Yeon-du.

57:01.167 --> 57:02.502
Yeon-du, it's Daddy.

57:02.585 --> 57:04.129
Yeon-du, open your eyes.

57:04.921 --> 57:06.214
[Mo-eum exhales]

57:06.297 --> 57:08.633
[Dan-ho whimpering] Yeon-du, Daddy's here.

57:08.716 --> 57:10.009
Yeon-du, open your eyes.

57:10.093 --> 57:12.887
Sir, can you step back for a moment?
We need to insert the IV.

57:12.971 --> 57:14.180
[Dan-ho] Okay.

57:21.396 --> 57:22.230
Yeon-du.

57:23.690 --> 57:24.899
Are you okay? Are you awake?

57:25.483 --> 57:27.527
Where are we? Who am I?

57:27.610 --> 57:29.112
The hospital.

57:30.363 --> 57:32.157
Daddy.

57:32.740 --> 57:35.326
[whimpering] Yeah, it's me.

57:36.369 --> 57:38.079
I'm here now. It's okay.

57:38.913 --> 57:39.998
Nothing's going to happen.

57:50.967 --> 57:52.343
[Myeong-u] Goodness.

57:53.511 --> 57:55.430
-Hey.
-[Myeong-u chuckling]

57:55.513 --> 57:58.183
Those clothes look better on you than me.

57:58.266 --> 58:00.310
Thanks for lending them to me.

58:00.393 --> 58:03.104
That was a big mess you made.

58:03.188 --> 58:04.856
That's okay. It happens.

58:04.939 --> 58:06.900
I'm sorry. I came and just caused trouble.

58:06.983 --> 58:08.943
Don't worry about it. It's no big deal.

58:09.027 --> 58:10.278
We can just throw it away.

58:10.361 --> 58:13.448
No, we can't!
It'd be such a waste to throw away.

58:14.199 --> 58:15.992
Maybe if I had no idea,

58:16.075 --> 58:19.662
but now I know just how much time
and effort went into making this.

58:19.746 --> 58:21.706
-How can we throw this away?
-[Myeong-u chuckles]

58:21.789 --> 58:25.126
Then, how about we eat the parts
not covered in dirt?

58:25.710 --> 58:28.755
[Myeong-u] We're not bums.
Why would we eat something off the ground?

58:28.838 --> 58:31.424
Okay! I'll see what I can do.

58:31.508 --> 58:33.676
We have to have a barbecue.
There's plenty of charcoal.

58:33.760 --> 58:35.053
You said your stomach hurt.

58:35.136 --> 58:38.556
It's meat. That's a cure-all.

58:38.640 --> 58:40.308
-[thunderclap]
-Did you hear that?

58:40.391 --> 58:42.685
See? The sky is angry.
It wants us to cook meat!

58:43.269 --> 58:44.604
I think it's going to rain.

58:44.687 --> 58:46.314
-On rainy days…
-[Myeong-u] Meat!

58:46.397 --> 58:48.066
We should have kalguksu!

58:49.734 --> 58:51.402
-Spicy kalguksu!
-[Myeong-u] What?

58:51.903 --> 58:52.904
[rain pattering]

58:56.157 --> 58:57.325
[upbeat music playing]

59:07.377 --> 59:08.211
-Mr. Yoon?
-Yeah?

59:08.294 --> 59:10.004
Prepare to be summoned.

59:10.880 --> 59:13.550
I'm going to report you
to the Ministry of Labor when we get back.

59:13.633 --> 59:17.220
Don't be so harsh.
I'm a victim too.

59:17.303 --> 59:18.763
Whatever.

59:18.846 --> 59:21.558
I can't do this. My hands hurt.

59:21.641 --> 59:22.850
Na-yun.

59:23.685 --> 59:27.188
Pretend the dough is someone you hate.

59:27.272 --> 59:28.481
It relieves your stress.

59:28.565 --> 59:31.442
And the dough gets chewy.
It kills two birds with one stone.

59:36.239 --> 59:38.700
-[pounds]
-One for Bae Seok-ryu?

59:38.783 --> 59:40.535
-[pounds]
-One for Jang Tae-hui?

59:41.619 --> 59:43.621
Yoon Myeong-u. One, two, three, four…

59:44.330 --> 59:46.708
Goodness. You're tearing it apart.

59:46.791 --> 59:49.043
Just kill me. That would be better.

59:49.127 --> 59:51.087
That's enough of your kitty punches.

59:51.921 --> 59:53.047
Goodness.

01:00:02.390 --> 01:00:03.224
[slurps]

01:00:06.477 --> 01:00:08.479
-[slurps]
-So does it taste all right?

01:00:08.563 --> 01:00:10.857
It's not just all right.

01:00:10.940 --> 01:00:12.400
It's really good. Right?

01:00:13.151 --> 01:00:15.069
The broth is especially insane.

01:00:15.153 --> 01:00:16.195
Really?

01:00:16.946 --> 01:00:18.323
Mr. Yoon, do you like it too?

01:00:18.406 --> 01:00:19.574
Seok-ryu.

01:00:20.283 --> 01:00:23.077
We don't need meat.
Doenjang was the answer.

01:00:23.745 --> 01:00:25.580
It's so warm and soothing.

01:00:25.663 --> 01:00:30.293
I tip my hat to the making
of Korean pastes and sauces.

01:00:30.376 --> 01:00:33.463
You wished for doenjang to disappear
when you were preparing it.

01:00:35.965 --> 01:00:39.469
But where did Seung-hyo go?
He's missing dinner.

01:00:39.552 --> 01:00:42.055
I don't know.
I called, but he didn't pick up.

01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:45.308
Just leave him.
He'll come back when he gets hungry.

01:00:45.850 --> 01:00:48.978
You've been so focused on us
that you haven't been able to eat.

01:00:49.062 --> 01:00:50.355
-You worked so hard on this.
-No.

01:00:50.438 --> 01:00:51.397
I'm eating fine.

01:00:52.607 --> 01:00:53.608
Na-yun.

01:00:54.567 --> 01:00:55.693
Do you want some more?

01:00:57.195 --> 01:00:58.738
Flour's fattening though.

01:00:59.739 --> 01:01:00.740
Just a little more.

01:01:01.324 --> 01:01:02.158
Okay. Here.

01:01:02.241 --> 01:01:04.118
-Can I have some more too?
-Hey.

01:01:04.202 --> 01:01:06.371
-Me too.
-Jeez. Then, me too.

01:01:06.454 --> 01:01:07.789
[all laughing]

01:01:07.872 --> 01:01:09.874
I'll bring the pot. Wait here.

01:01:12.251 --> 01:01:14.379
[Myeong-u giggles]
If it's good, then it's fine!

01:01:14.879 --> 01:01:18.091
-[Hyeong-chan] Give it here. I'll take it.
-[Seok-ryu] No, that's okay.

01:01:18.633 --> 01:01:21.469
[Myeong-u] This looks good.
Wow! [chuckles]

01:01:34.107 --> 01:01:35.274
Seok-ryu!

01:01:36.025 --> 01:01:37.485
I'll do it. You can stop now.

01:01:38.194 --> 01:01:40.405
We can't have the cook
clean the dishes too.

01:01:40.488 --> 01:01:43.408
I lost in rock, paper, scissors
fair and square.

01:01:43.825 --> 01:01:46.202
And I broke your jar.
I should make up for that.

01:01:47.995 --> 01:01:48.996
You're right.

01:01:50.581 --> 01:01:52.375
But will that be enough?

01:01:53.668 --> 01:01:54.711
A single onggi of mine

01:01:54.836 --> 01:01:56.504
-cost more than a million won.
-[exclaims]

01:01:57.672 --> 01:01:58.673
So close.

01:01:59.465 --> 01:02:00.967
I could've used you for another day.

01:02:01.050 --> 01:02:02.009
[chuckles softly]

01:02:02.093 --> 01:02:04.595
Send me your bank account number.
I'll reimburse you.

01:02:05.263 --> 01:02:06.222
Send me yours too.

01:02:07.223 --> 01:02:08.808
-Your recipe.
-What?

01:02:09.308 --> 01:02:11.936
For the spicy kalguksu.
Let's call it even with that.

01:02:12.562 --> 01:02:14.439
I haven't had noodles
that good in so long.

01:02:14.522 --> 01:02:17.233
It's really easy to make.

01:02:17.316 --> 01:02:19.444
You saw the ingredients earlier.

01:02:19.527 --> 01:02:21.154
The seasoning is important.

01:02:21.237 --> 01:02:23.573
It's three parts gochujang,
one part doenjang.

01:02:23.656 --> 01:02:25.908
Three spoonfuls of gochujang
per spoonful of doenjang.

01:02:25.992 --> 01:02:28.077
How big is a spoonful?

01:02:29.412 --> 01:02:30.621
[water splashing]

01:02:30.705 --> 01:02:31.581
Is it this much?

01:02:34.917 --> 01:02:36.002
[chuckles softly]

01:02:36.085 --> 01:02:39.589
I see. You know nothing.

01:02:40.339 --> 01:02:42.633
We've got a long way to go.

01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:51.642
I was going to scold her parents
when they came.

01:02:52.435 --> 01:02:53.561
You're her father?

01:02:54.854 --> 01:02:56.105
I'm sorry.

01:02:56.731 --> 01:02:58.441
You don't have to apologize to me.

01:02:59.525 --> 01:03:00.818
You should apologize to Yeon-du.

01:03:01.986 --> 01:03:05.656
How could you leave a sick kid home alone?

01:03:05.740 --> 01:03:08.785
How could you let a five-year-old
call 119 on her own?

01:03:11.078 --> 01:03:12.663
I have no excuse.

01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:15.625
You said you were covering a story.

01:03:15.708 --> 01:03:17.418
Are you going to change the world?

01:03:17.710 --> 01:03:19.003
Are you saving the country?

01:03:19.712 --> 01:03:22.381
How can you accomplish anything
if you can't take care of your kid?

01:03:25.218 --> 01:03:26.385
Yeon-du

01:03:26.469 --> 01:03:28.262
was alone when I saw her last time.

01:03:29.347 --> 01:03:32.016
She had this in her hand
as she was alone again today.

01:03:32.850 --> 01:03:33.684
[exhales]

01:03:37.814 --> 01:03:39.565
[mellow music playing]

01:03:44.987 --> 01:03:46.113
[crying]

01:03:51.452 --> 01:03:52.286
[sniffles]

01:03:54.705 --> 01:03:57.458
Yeon-du, are you okay? Does anything hurt?

01:03:58.000 --> 01:03:59.168
Hey, Yeon-du.

01:03:59.252 --> 01:04:00.920
Were you brave for your tests?

01:04:01.003 --> 01:04:02.338
Don't yell at my dad.

01:04:03.047 --> 01:04:03.881
[Mo-eum] What?

01:04:03.965 --> 01:04:06.968
I hate people who yell at my dad.

01:04:07.051 --> 01:04:09.178
Yeon-du, it's not like that.

01:04:09.262 --> 01:04:11.430
She didn't do anything wrong.

01:04:12.139 --> 01:04:15.101
From now on,
I'm going to ignore you when I see you.

01:04:15.643 --> 01:04:17.311
Don't ever talk to me again.

01:04:17.395 --> 01:04:18.563
[exhales]

01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:42.295
Yeon-du, were you scared
on your own earlier?

01:04:43.671 --> 01:04:44.755
[Yeon-du] No.

01:04:45.339 --> 01:04:47.216
You taught me.

01:04:48.759 --> 01:04:51.470
Call 112 when I meet a bad person.

01:04:52.430 --> 01:04:54.348
Call 119 when I'm hurt.

01:04:57.727 --> 01:04:58.769
I'm sorry.

01:05:01.355 --> 01:05:03.107
Yeon-du,

01:05:04.066 --> 01:05:05.443
I'm so sorry.

01:05:07.236 --> 01:05:08.946
I'm sorry too.

01:05:10.323 --> 01:05:12.158
Why would you be sorry?

01:05:12.992 --> 01:05:16.412
I was looking for crop circles.

01:05:17.288 --> 01:05:21.918
But you brought me a four-leaf clover,
so I yelled at you. I'm sorry.

01:05:27.173 --> 01:05:28.633
It's okay.

01:05:39.101 --> 01:05:40.770
Did you make all of these too?

01:05:41.437 --> 01:05:42.438
Yeah.

01:05:43.105 --> 01:05:44.106
That's so cool.

01:05:50.488 --> 01:05:53.407
-I have a lot of scars, don't I?
-I'm sorry for being rude.

01:05:53.491 --> 01:05:55.618
What? Not at all.

01:05:55.701 --> 01:05:57.954
I'm proud of them. I wanted to show you.

01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:02.041
They're marks of my dream.

01:06:05.628 --> 01:06:09.590
When I look at them, they remind me
my passion for onggi was quite intense.

01:06:09.674 --> 01:06:10.967
I'm fond of them.

01:06:12.259 --> 01:06:15.763
Now, they're just like tattoos.
[chuckles softly]

01:06:19.934 --> 01:06:24.188
When did you decide
that you wanted to make onggi?

01:06:25.231 --> 01:06:28.651
Remember how I said
my dad was a doenjang master?

01:06:29.735 --> 01:06:31.821
I grew up around these onggi jars.

01:06:32.863 --> 01:06:36.659
They looked so crude and ugly at first.

01:06:37.368 --> 01:06:38.619
I wanted to store the pastes

01:06:38.786 --> 01:06:43.499
in something elegant,
like celadon or porcelain.

01:06:43.582 --> 01:06:46.210
But then, I slowly started to like onggi.

01:06:47.712 --> 01:06:50.506
Crocks, water jars, and liquor jars.

01:06:51.340 --> 01:06:53.843
Compared to decorative ceramics,

01:06:53.926 --> 01:06:56.846
practical bowls and jars used by people
looked more beautiful.

01:06:58.681 --> 01:07:01.225
That's why I started.
Pretty boring, right?

01:07:01.308 --> 01:07:02.268
No.

01:07:03.310 --> 01:07:07.440
To me, the stories of people who have
found their dreams always sound special.

01:07:08.607 --> 01:07:10.943
I have no idea where or how to start.

01:07:13.279 --> 01:07:14.822
What do you like?

01:07:14.905 --> 01:07:16.032
Sorry?

01:07:16.115 --> 01:07:18.075
It seems you're thinking about it
too seriously.

01:07:19.243 --> 01:07:22.329
Just go do what you've always liked doing,
whatever it may be.

01:07:23.831 --> 01:07:25.458
What I've always liked?

01:07:28.002 --> 01:07:29.837
When the food was being served,

01:07:30.671 --> 01:07:32.256
my bowls looked really pretty.

01:07:46.228 --> 01:07:47.313
There you are.

01:07:48.439 --> 01:07:51.692
Yeah, it's nice here.
The breeze feels cool too.

01:07:52.276 --> 01:07:54.278
You don't know what you're saying.

01:07:54.361 --> 01:07:56.781
It's hard to even stand here
when the fire's at its hottest.

01:07:57.490 --> 01:07:58.657
I suppose so.

01:08:14.173 --> 01:08:16.008
Do you remember when Seok-ryu said

01:08:16.634 --> 01:08:18.719
that we were passionate in the past?

01:08:19.470 --> 01:08:20.888
But we weren't.

01:08:21.472 --> 01:08:22.556
It was only me.

01:08:24.433 --> 01:08:26.936
My love was as hot as a burning kiln,

01:08:27.019 --> 01:08:29.063
but you were a low flame on a gas stove.

01:08:30.106 --> 01:08:34.235
It wasn't even hot enough
to cook an egg, let alone a bowl.

01:08:37.363 --> 01:08:39.031
Is that why you broke up with me?

01:08:39.824 --> 01:08:40.950
Yeah.

01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:44.328
I found a man
whose love burned hot.

01:08:45.830 --> 01:08:47.373
But do you know what's funny?

01:08:47.957 --> 01:08:49.333
I broke up with you,

01:08:50.793 --> 01:08:52.461
but it felt like you dumped me.

01:08:52.545 --> 01:08:53.879
That's not true.

01:08:55.214 --> 01:08:57.258
I took it hard too.

01:08:57.341 --> 01:08:58.843
I'm glad to hear that.

01:09:00.553 --> 01:09:05.099
I had always hoped
that you would seethe because of me.

01:09:07.101 --> 01:09:08.352
You'd lose your temper.

01:09:08.435 --> 01:09:11.105
You'd be foolish
since you couldn't control your emotions.

01:09:12.189 --> 01:09:15.985
After breaking up, you'd pathetically send
a text and ask, "Are you awake?"

01:09:18.237 --> 01:09:21.991
I almost texted you once. I was drunk.

01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:27.454
[clears throat]

01:09:29.248 --> 01:09:30.416
But earlier,

01:09:31.667 --> 01:09:32.668
you were so angry.

01:09:33.919 --> 01:09:36.463
You yelled at Seok-ryu
and embarrassed her.

01:09:36.547 --> 01:09:38.549
I've never seen you do that before.

01:09:38.632 --> 01:09:41.385
That's because she messed up.

01:09:41.468 --> 01:09:43.262
She didn't do anything wrong.

01:09:44.972 --> 01:09:46.307
To tell you the truth,

01:09:47.600 --> 01:09:48.684
that jar was cracked.

01:09:51.061 --> 01:09:53.647
I was going to move it
to the studio to repair it.

01:09:55.524 --> 01:09:57.359
I didn't want to be honest about it.

01:09:59.111 --> 01:10:00.529
I think…

01:10:02.281 --> 01:10:03.908
I was jealous.

01:10:06.493 --> 01:10:08.412
[pleasant music playing]

01:10:11.832 --> 01:10:12.917
[snoring]

01:10:19.548 --> 01:10:21.467
[pop song playing]

01:11:22.778 --> 01:11:24.655
When did he take those?

01:12:01.400 --> 01:12:02.318
[sniffles]

01:12:06.405 --> 01:12:07.823
Why are you out here this late?

01:12:08.574 --> 01:12:10.534
I should ask you the same thing.

01:12:10.617 --> 01:12:11.910
I couldn't sleep, so I came out.

01:12:11.994 --> 01:12:13.954
I saw something white moving outside.

01:12:14.038 --> 01:12:16.165
That's because you didn't eat dinner.

01:12:17.541 --> 01:12:20.544
There's some dough left.
Do you want some kalguksu?

01:12:21.628 --> 01:12:22.755
Later.

01:12:24.882 --> 01:12:29.011
Hey, you got the stain out of my shirt.
What did you use?

01:12:29.094 --> 01:12:30.387
Rice and vinegar.

01:12:34.183 --> 01:12:36.643
[chuckles softly]
How kind and thoughtful of you.

01:12:40.564 --> 01:12:42.608
But why do you keep opening those lids?

01:12:43.359 --> 01:12:44.818
I'm looking for treasure.

01:12:46.612 --> 01:12:49.656
I heard one of these has soy sauce
that's been aged for 100 years.

01:12:50.407 --> 01:12:51.408
Soy sauce?

01:12:52.117 --> 01:12:53.369
Why are you looking for that?

01:12:53.452 --> 01:12:55.120
I'm curious.

01:12:55.204 --> 01:12:59.333
I wonder what soy sauce looks like
after being aged for 100 years.

01:13:00.834 --> 01:13:04.254
Still, there are so many jars here.
It'll take ages to open them all.

01:13:04.338 --> 01:13:07.007
I'll open them, so mind your own business.

01:13:12.638 --> 01:13:15.349
How is this soy sauce
different from others?

01:13:15.432 --> 01:13:19.937
One of the old ladies
said it's darker and smells richer.

01:13:20.020 --> 01:13:21.522
It's still just soy sauce.

01:13:21.605 --> 01:13:25.317
How will you remember what you've opened
if you search randomly like this?

01:13:25.401 --> 01:13:27.236
You take that side. I'll look here.

01:13:28.445 --> 01:13:29.613
Why are you helping me?

01:13:31.490 --> 01:13:33.867
You're always trying
to bite my head off these days.

01:13:35.160 --> 01:13:37.204
-When did I do that?
-All the time.

01:13:38.163 --> 01:13:40.457
You pick fights with me
and get irritable for no reason.

01:13:40.541 --> 01:13:43.794
-You're always scolding me.
-Jeez. You're being ridiculous.

01:13:43.877 --> 01:13:44.920
[clears throat, sniffles]

01:13:45.003 --> 01:13:47.881
[Seok-ryu] You wait and see.

01:13:48.549 --> 01:13:50.884
This is gochujang.

01:13:52.177 --> 01:13:53.053
[exclaims]

01:13:53.137 --> 01:13:54.847
This one's doenjang. Darn.

01:13:56.598 --> 01:13:57.891
It's soy sauce.

01:13:59.518 --> 01:14:00.602
What? You found it already?

01:14:06.650 --> 01:14:07.484
Oh.

01:14:08.026 --> 01:14:08.861
[chuckles softly]

01:14:09.486 --> 01:14:12.948
Hey, it does look a little darker.

01:14:13.031 --> 01:14:14.616
It's amazing.

01:14:15.200 --> 01:14:16.118
What is?

01:14:16.201 --> 01:14:18.036
This jar…

01:14:20.038 --> 01:14:21.790
is filled with the night sky.

01:14:23.167 --> 01:14:24.626
It's so dark.

01:14:25.419 --> 01:14:26.628
It's sparkling.

01:14:28.005 --> 01:14:31.383
I thought you were looking for soy sauce.
What's with the poem?

01:14:33.343 --> 01:14:35.971
Spicy noodles. Wild chives and soy sauce.

01:14:37.514 --> 01:14:38.765
Pickled perilla leaves.

01:14:39.266 --> 01:14:42.019
Why are you suddenly talking about food?
Are you hungry?

01:14:42.102 --> 01:14:43.061
[chuckles softly]

01:14:44.563 --> 01:14:45.606
Hey, Choisseung.

01:14:47.065 --> 01:14:48.150
I think I found it.

01:14:48.734 --> 01:14:50.986
Yeah. This is the soy sauce, right?

01:14:51.069 --> 01:14:54.907
I mean, a dream doesn't have to be grand
or elaborate.

01:14:56.158 --> 01:14:59.703
I can't do anything impressive,
like how you swim the freestyle,

01:15:01.163 --> 01:15:04.291
but I think I can manage the dog paddle.

01:15:07.169 --> 01:15:08.128
I…

01:15:09.630 --> 01:15:10.672
want to cook.

01:15:16.845 --> 01:15:18.222
[mellow music playing]

01:15:18.305 --> 01:15:22.100
Hey, there are so many things
I want to make with this.

01:15:23.268 --> 01:15:26.230
[Tae-hui] I think I was jealous.

01:15:28.190 --> 01:15:29.942
When you're with Seok-ryu,

01:15:30.651 --> 01:15:33.070
you're not the person I used to know.

01:15:33.153 --> 01:15:36.323
You're irritable and not generous either.

01:15:37.115 --> 01:15:39.076
You're pathetic and immature.

01:15:40.577 --> 01:15:42.412
And you're always looking
in her direction.

01:15:46.083 --> 01:15:46.917
[exhales]

01:15:47.000 --> 01:15:49.336
Do you know how you look
when you look at her?

01:15:51.964 --> 01:15:54.633
You're just full of curiosity, aren't you?

01:15:54.716 --> 01:15:56.260
[Seok-ryu] That's just how I am.

01:15:57.803 --> 01:15:59.054
[Tae-hui] You smile.

01:16:02.349 --> 01:16:03.642
When Seok-ryu smiles,

01:16:06.228 --> 01:16:07.688
you just smile with her.

01:16:10.274 --> 01:16:11.858
[Seok-ryu] I've never done it before,

01:16:11.942 --> 01:16:15.487
but if I made soy sauce marinated crabs
with this, it would be awesome, right?

01:16:16.113 --> 01:16:18.615
Should I ask her
for a taste of this tomorrow?

01:16:19.575 --> 01:16:22.953
Even the smallest difference
can make a big impact, you know?

01:16:24.746 --> 01:16:27.499
[Seung-hyo] I've been running away
from my feelings for a long time.

01:16:28.333 --> 01:16:31.503
I've ignored and denied them.

01:16:32.087 --> 01:16:33.046
But…

01:16:33.839 --> 01:16:39.344
after seeing Seok-ryu smile so brightly
in front of me now, I realized.

01:16:39.720 --> 01:16:40.721
I…

01:16:42.806 --> 01:16:44.933
can't help but like her.

01:16:45.851 --> 01:16:47.436
[muted conversation]

01:17:00.657 --> 01:17:07.623
GO BACK TO YOU

01:17:08.707 --> 01:17:09.916
[pop song playing]

01:17:41.365 --> 01:17:45.577
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:17:45.661 --> 01:17:47.537
[Seung-hyo] I've known her for so long.

01:17:48.163 --> 01:17:49.998
I thought I knew everything about her.

01:17:50.749 --> 01:17:53.085
[Seok-ryu] What if I became
a cook like my dad?

01:17:53.752 --> 01:17:56.338
[Seung-hyo] I thought I'd moved on
from my feelings for her.

01:17:56.963 --> 01:17:59.216
But I'm a bit confused
after seeing her again.

01:17:59.299 --> 01:18:02.135
I've never confessed
my feelings to her before.

01:18:02.219 --> 01:18:05.305
[In-suk] Men staying out late enough
to see the morning dew is a big problem!

01:18:05.389 --> 01:18:08.350
[Seung-hyo] I saw you.
You were with some woman.

01:18:08.433 --> 01:18:10.769
[Mi-suk] Where did you go off
after closing the shop?

01:18:10.852 --> 01:18:12.187
Are you having an affair?

01:18:12.938 --> 01:18:15.023
[Seok-ryu] You've been distant
lately towards me.

01:18:15.649 --> 01:18:18.527
I feel like I'm going to
lose my mind because of you!

01:18:22.072 --> 01:18:25.075
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
